window.I15_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Linguistics & Language Structure 語言學與語言結構","cards":[{"w":"linguistics","p":"n.","d":"the scientific study of language","c":"語言學","s":"My cousin decided to study linguistics at university because she loves languages, and she wants to understand how children learn to speak.","t":"我的表姊決定在大學念語言學，因為她熱愛語言，而且她想了解孩子是如何學會說話的。"},{"w":"linguist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies how languages work","c":"語言學家","s":"The linguist recorded the old villagers telling stories, and she later used the recordings to describe the grammar of their language.","t":"這位語言學家錄下了年長村民講故事的聲音，之後她用這些錄音來描述他們語言的文法。"},{"w":"linguistic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with language","c":"語言的","s":"Moving to Japan was a big linguistic challenge for Tom, but he practised every day and could chat with neighbours after a year.","t":"搬到日本對湯姆來說是一大語言上的挑戰，但他每天練習，一年後就能和鄰居聊天了。"},{"w":"sociolinguistics","p":"n.","d":"the study of how language and society affect each other","c":"社會語言學","s":"In our sociolinguistics class we compared how teenagers and grandparents speak, and we found that each group uses very different words.","t":"在我們的社會語言學課上，我們比較了青少年和祖父母說話的方式，結果發現每個族群使用的詞彙都非常不同。"},{"w":"psycholinguistics","p":"n.","d":"the study of how the mind uses and understands language","c":"心理語言學","s":"Researchers in psycholinguistics use eye-tracking cameras, because they want to know exactly how our brains process words while we read.","t":"心理語言學的研究人員使用眼動追蹤攝影機，因為他們想確切知道我們閱讀時大腦是如何處理文字的。"},{"w":"phonetics","p":"n.","d":"the study of speech sounds","c":"語音學","s":"Our teacher studied phonetics in college, so she can explain exactly where to put our tongue when we make the \"th\" sound.","t":"我們的老師在大學學過語音學，所以她能確切解釋我們發「th」音時舌頭該放在哪裡。"},{"w":"semantics","p":"n.","d":"the study of the meaning of words and sentences","c":"語意學","s":"\"Cheap\" and \"inexpensive\" seem to mean the same thing, but semantics shows us that one word can sound more negative than the other.","t":"「cheap」和「inexpensive」看似意思相同，但語意學告訴我們其中一個字聽起來可能比另一個更負面。"},{"w":"pragmatics","p":"n.","d":"the study of how context changes what we mean","c":"語用學","s":"When my mum asks \"Is the door open?\", she usually wants me to close it, and pragmatics explains how we understand these hidden requests.","t":"當我媽媽問「門開著嗎？」時，她通常是要我去關門，而語用學解釋了我們如何理解這些隱藏的請求。"},{"w":"corpus","p":"n.","d":"a large collection of real texts used for language study","c":"語料庫","s":"The dictionary team searched a huge corpus of newspapers and websites, so they could see how often people really use each word.","t":"字典編輯團隊搜尋了一個由報紙和網站組成的龐大語料庫，以便了解人們實際上多常使用每個字。"},{"w":"morpheme","p":"n.","d":"the smallest part of a word that has meaning","c":"詞素","s":"The word \"unhappy\" has two parts, and each morpheme adds meaning, because \"un\" means \"not\" and \"happy\" means \"glad\".","t":"「unhappy」這個字有兩個部分，而每個詞素都增加了意思，因為「un」表示「不」，「happy」表示「高興」。"},{"w":"phoneme","p":"n.","d":"one of the smallest sound units in a language","c":"音素","s":"English learners in Taiwan often mix up the sounds in \"light\" and \"right\", because each phoneme does not exist separately in their first language.","t":"台灣的英語學習者常常混淆「light」和「right」的發音，因為這兩個音素在他們的母語中並沒有分開存在。"},{"w":"syllable","p":"n.","d":"a part of a word with one vowel sound","c":"音節","s":"The word \"banana\" has three syllable, and English speakers usually put the strongest sound on the middle one.","t":"「banana」這個字有三個音節，而說英語的人通常把最重的音放在中間那個上。"},{"w":"prefix","p":"n.","d":"letters added to the start of a word to change its meaning","c":"字首","s":"If you add the prefix \"re\" to \"write\", you get \"rewrite\", and the new word means \"write again\".","t":"如果你在「write」前面加上字首「re」，就會得到「rewrite」，而這個新字的意思是「再寫一次」。"},{"w":"suffix","p":"n.","d":"letters added to the end of a word","c":"字尾","s":"The suffix \"ness\" turns adjectives into nouns, so \"kind\" becomes \"kindness\" and \"dark\" becomes \"darkness\".","t":"字尾「ness」能把形容詞變成名詞，所以「kind」變成「kindness」，「dark」變成「darkness」。"},{"w":"affix","p":"n.","d":"a prefix or a suffix","c":"詞綴","s":"Learning one common affix can help you guess hundreds of new words, because the same pieces appear again and again.","t":"學會一個常見的詞綴能幫你猜出幾百個新字，因為同樣的部分會一再出現。"},{"w":"word root","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main part of a word that carries its basic meaning","c":"字根","s":"The word root \"port\" means \"carry\", so once you know it, words like \"transport\" and \"export\" become much easier to remember.","t":"字根「port」的意思是「攜帶」，所以一旦你知道它，像「transport」和「export」這樣的字就變得容易記多了。"},{"w":"inflection","p":"n.","d":"a change in a word's ending to show tense, number, etc.","c":"字尾變化；詞形變化","s":"English adds an inflection like \"-s\" or \"-ed\" to many words, but Chinese verbs never change their form at all.","t":"英文會在許多字後面加上像「-s」或「-ed」這樣的詞形變化，但中文的動詞完全不會改變形式。"},{"w":"compound word","p":"n.phr.","d":"a word made from two or more words","c":"複合字","s":"\"Toothbrush\" is a compound word made from \"tooth\" and \"brush\", and German has even longer examples than English.","t":"「toothbrush」是由「tooth」和「brush」組成的複合字，而德文的例子甚至比英文還要長。"},{"w":"word order","p":"n.phr.","d":"the order in which words are arranged in a sentence","c":"詞序；字序","s":"In English the word order is usually subject, verb, object, but in Japanese the verb normally comes at the end.","t":"英文的詞序通常是主詞、動詞、受詞，但在日文中，動詞通常出現在句尾。"},{"w":"sentence structure","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way words are put together to form a sentence","c":"句子結構","s":"My writing teacher told me to vary my sentence structure, because using only short simple sentences makes an essay sound boring.","t":"我的寫作老師叫我變化句子結構，因為只用短的簡單句會讓文章聽起來很無聊。"},{"w":"grammar","p":"n.","d":"the rules for forming words and sentences","c":"文法","s":"Many students hate learning grammar rules, but these rules help them write clearly and avoid confusing their readers.","t":"許多學生討厭學文法規則，但這些規則能幫助他們寫得清楚，並避免讓讀者感到困惑。"},{"w":"grammatical","p":"adj.","d":"following or connected with the rules of grammar","c":"文法上的","s":"The essay had a few grammatical mistakes, but the ideas were so interesting that the teacher still gave it a high score.","t":"這篇文章有幾個文法上的錯誤，但內容想法非常有趣，所以老師還是給了高分。"},{"w":"prescriptive","p":"adj.","d":"telling people how they should use language","c":"規範性的","s":"Old grammar books were very prescriptive and told readers never to end a sentence with a preposition, but modern writers often ignore that rule.","t":"舊的文法書非常規範性，告訴讀者絕對不要用介系詞結束句子，但現代作家常常忽略這條規則。"},{"w":"ungrammatical","p":"adj.","d":"not following the rules of grammar","c":"不合文法的","s":"The sentence \"He go to school yesterday\" is ungrammatical, so the teacher circled it and asked the student to correct the verb.","t":"「He go to school yesterday」這個句子是不合文法的，所以老師把它圈起來，要求學生改正動詞。"},{"w":"part of speech","p":"n.phr.","d":"a word class such as noun, verb or adjective","c":"詞性","s":"\"Light\" can be a noun, a verb or an adjective, so you must check the sentence to decide its part of speech.","t":"「light」可以是名詞、動詞或形容詞，所以你必須查看句子才能決定它的詞性。"},{"w":"cognate","p":"n.","d":"a word that has the same origin as a word in another language","c":"同源字","s":"The English word \"night\" and the German word \"Nacht\" are cognate, and that is why they look and sound so similar.","t":"英文字「night」和德文字「Nacht」是同源字，這就是為什麼它們看起來、聽起來都那麼相似。"},{"w":"plural","p":"n.","d":"the form of a word that means more than one","c":"複數形","s":"Most English nouns add \"s\" to form the plural, but some, like \"child\" and \"mouse\", change in strange ways.","t":"大多數英文名詞加「s」構成複數形，但有些字，像「child」和「mouse」，會以奇怪的方式改變。"},{"w":"singular","p":"adj.","d":"showing only one person or thing","c":"單數的","s":"\"News\" looks like a plural noun, but it is actually singular, so we say \"the news is good\" and not \"the news are good\".","t":"「news」看起來像複數名詞，但它其實是單數的，所以我們說「the news is good」而不是「the news are good」。"},{"w":"passive voice","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sentence form where the subject receives the action","c":"被動語態","s":"Science reports often use the passive voice, so writers say \"the water was heated\" instead of \"we heated the water\".","t":"科學報告常常使用被動語態，所以作者會說「水被加熱了」而不是「我們加熱了水」。"},{"w":"conjugate","p":"v.","d":"to list or change the forms of a verb","c":"（動詞）變化詞形","s":"In Spanish class we had to conjugate twenty verbs every week, and I often forgot the endings for \"we\" and \"they\".","t":"在西班牙文課上，我們每週都必須變化二十個動詞的詞形，而我常常忘記「我們」和「他們」的字尾。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Sounds, Speech & Accents 語音、口說與口音","cards":[{"w":"accent","p":"n.","d":"a way of pronouncing a language that shows where you are from","c":"口音","s":"My new classmate has a strong Scottish accent, so at first I found him hard to understand, but now I enjoy listening to him.","t":"我的新同學有很重的蘇格蘭口音，所以一開始我覺得他的話很難懂，但現在我很喜歡聽他說話。"},{"w":"dialect","p":"n.","d":"a form of a language spoken in one area or by one group","c":"方言","s":"My grandparents speak a local dialect at home, while my parents usually speak Mandarin with me and my sister.","t":"我的祖父母在家說當地的方言，而我的父母通常用國語和我及我妹妹說話。"},{"w":"intonation","p":"n.","d":"the rise and fall of the voice when speaking","c":"語調","s":"If you say \"Really?\" with a rising intonation, it sounds like a question, but a falling tone can make it sound bored.","t":"如果你用上揚的語調說「Really?」，聽起來就像個問題，但下降的語調會讓它聽起來很無聊。"},{"w":"vowel","p":"n.","d":"a sound like a, e, i, o or u","c":"母音","s":"English has many more vowel sounds than Japanese, so Japanese learners often find words like \"ship\" and \"sheep\" confusing.","t":"英文的母音比日文多得多，所以日本學習者常常覺得像「ship」和「sheep」這樣的字很容易搞混。"},{"w":"consonant","p":"n.","d":"a speech sound that is not a vowel, like b, t or s","c":"子音","s":"Some words begin with three consonant in a row, like \"street\" and \"spring\", and these clusters are hard for many learners to say.","t":"有些字開頭連續有三個子音，像「street」和「spring」，而這些子音群對很多學習者來說很難發音。"},{"w":"rhythm","p":"n.","d":"a regular pattern of strong and weak sounds","c":"節奏","s":"English has a bouncing rhythm with strong and weak beats, so reading poems aloud is a good way to practise it.","t":"英文有一種強弱拍交替的跳躍節奏，所以大聲朗讀詩是練習它的好方法。"},{"w":"pitch","p":"n.","d":"how high or low a sound is","c":"音高","s":"In Mandarin the pitch of your voice can change a word's meaning, so \"mā\" and \"mà\" are completely different words.","t":"在中文裡，聲音的音高可以改變一個字的意思，所以「媽」和「罵」是完全不同的字。"},{"w":"stutter","p":"v.","d":"to repeat sounds because it is hard to speak smoothly","c":"口吃；結巴","s":"He used to stutter when he felt nervous, but speech lessons gave him confidence, and now he hosts the school radio show.","t":"他以前緊張時會結巴，但說話課程給了他信心，現在他主持學校的廣播節目。"},{"w":"mumble","p":"v.","d":"to speak quietly and unclearly","c":"含糊地說","s":"Please don't mumble during your presentation, because the students at the back of the hall need to hear every word.","t":"請不要在報告時含糊地說話，因為禮堂後面的學生需要聽清楚每一個字。"},{"w":"whisper","p":"v.","d":"to speak very softly using your breath","c":"低聲說；耳語","s":"We had to whisper in the library, but my friend kept laughing loudly, so the librarian asked us to leave.","t":"我們在圖書館裡必須低聲說話，但我朋友一直大聲笑，所以圖書館員請我們離開。"},{"w":"pronounce","p":"v.","d":"to make the sound of a word","c":"發音","s":"Many people do not know how to pronounce \"Wednesday\", because the first \"d\" is silent and the spelling looks very strange.","t":"很多人不知道「Wednesday」怎麼發音，因為第一個「d」不發音，而且拼字看起來很奇怪。"},{"w":"mispronounce","p":"v.","d":"to say a word wrongly","c":"發錯音","s":"The host mispronounce the singer's name twice, and the audience laughed, so he apologised and asked her to say it herself.","t":"主持人把歌手的名字唸錯了兩次，觀眾都笑了，所以他道歉並請她自己說一次。"},{"w":"vocal cords","p":"n.phr.","d":"parts in your throat that make the sound of your voice","c":"聲帶","s":"Singers rest their vocal cords before a big concert, because shouting or talking too much can damage their voice.","t":"歌手在大型演唱會前會讓聲帶休息，因為大叫或說太多話會傷害他們的嗓子。"},{"w":"tongue twister","p":"n.phr.","d":"a phrase that is difficult to say quickly","c":"繞口令","s":"Our teacher starts each class with a tongue twister like \"She sells seashells\", and we all laugh when we make mistakes.","t":"我們老師每堂課都用一個像「She sells seashells」這樣的繞口令開始，而我們犯錯時大家都會大笑。"},{"w":"lisp","p":"n.","d":"a speech problem where \"s\" sounds like \"th\"","c":"大舌頭（s 發成 th）","s":"The little boy had a lisp, so \"sun\" sounded like \"thun\", but it disappeared after he got his new front teeth.","t":"那個小男孩有大舌頭，所以「sun」聽起來像「thun」，但他長出新門牙後這個問題就消失了。"},{"w":"fluent","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak a language easily and well","c":"流利的","s":"Sara became fluent in French after living in Paris for two years, and now she works as a tour guide there.","t":"莎拉在巴黎住了兩年後，法文變得流利，現在她在那裡當導遊。"},{"w":"rhyme","p":"v.","d":"to have the same ending sound","c":"押韻","s":"Children's songs are easy to remember because the lines often rhyme, like \"cat\" and \"hat\" or \"star\" and \"far\".","t":"兒歌很容易記住，因為歌詞常常押韻，像「cat」和「hat」或「star」和「far」。"},{"w":"silent letter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a letter that is written but not pronounced","c":"不發音字母","s":"The \"k\" in \"knife\" is a silent letter, so we say \"nife\", which often surprises young learners.","t":"「knife」中的「k」是不發音字母，所以我們唸成「nife」，這常常讓年幼的學習者感到驚訝。"},{"w":"phonetic alphabet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a set of symbols that show speech sounds","c":"音標","s":"Most good dictionaries show words in the international phonetic alphabet, so you can check the pronunciation even without audio.","t":"大多數好的字典會用國際音標標示單字，所以即使沒有音檔，你也能查到發音。"},{"w":"native speaker","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who learned a language from birth","c":"母語人士","s":"Talking with a native speaker helped me learn natural expressions, but I also learned a lot from other learners in my class.","t":"和母語人士交談幫助我學到自然的說法，但我也從班上其他學習者身上學到很多。"},{"w":"mother tongue","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first language you learned as a child","c":"母語","s":"Her mother tongue is Hakka, but she also speaks Mandarin, English and a little Korean, so she often helps foreign tourists.","t":"她的母語是客家話，但她也會說國語、英文和一點韓文，所以她常常幫助外國觀光客。"},{"w":"second language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language you learn after your first one","c":"第二語言","s":"English is a second language for millions of people in Asia, and many of them use it every day at work.","t":"英文是亞洲數百萬人的第二語言，而且其中許多人每天在工作中使用它。"},{"w":"monotone","p":"n.","d":"a voice that stays on one level and sounds dull","c":"單調的聲音","s":"The lecturer spoke in a monotone for the whole hour, so half the students fell asleep before he finished.","t":"那位講師整整一小時都用單調的聲音說話，所以一半的學生在他講完前就睡著了。"},{"w":"lip-reading","p":"n.","d":"understanding speech by watching people's lips","c":"讀唇","s":"My aunt cannot hear well, but she is very good at lip-reading, so please look at her when you speak.","t":"我阿姨聽力不好，但她很擅長讀唇，所以你說話時請看著她。"},{"w":"speech therapist","p":"n.phr.","d":"a professional who helps people speak more clearly","c":"語言治療師","s":"The speech therapist taught my brother some fun mouth exercises, and his speech became much clearer within a few months.","t":"語言治療師教了我弟弟一些有趣的嘴部運動，而他的說話在幾個月內就清楚多了。"},{"w":"speech recognition","p":"n.phr.","d":"technology that changes spoken words into text","c":"語音辨識","s":"The speech recognition on my phone works well in quiet rooms, but it often writes the wrong words on a noisy bus.","t":"我手機上的語音辨識在安靜的房間裡運作良好，但在吵雜的公車上常常打出錯字。"},{"w":"aloud","p":"adv.","d":"in a voice that others can hear","c":"出聲地；大聲地","s":"Reading stories aloud to young children builds their vocabulary, and it also helps parents and kids feel closer.","t":"為幼兒大聲朗讀故事能增加他們的詞彙量，而且也能讓父母和孩子感覺更親近。"},{"w":"audible","p":"adj.","d":"loud enough to be heard","c":"聽得見的","s":"The speaker's voice was barely audible because the microphone was broken, so people at the back started to complain.","t":"因為麥克風壞了，講者的聲音幾乎聽不太見，所以後面的人開始抱怨。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Words, Meaning & Usage 詞彙、語意與用法","cards":[{"w":"synonym","p":"n.","d":"a word with the same or a similar meaning","c":"同義字","s":"\"Big\" is a synonym for \"large\", but writers often choose \"huge\" or \"enormous\" when they want a stronger effect.","t":"「big」是「large」的同義字，但當作者想要更強的效果時，常會選擇「huge」或「enormous」。"},{"w":"antonym","p":"n.","d":"a word with the opposite meaning","c":"反義字","s":"The antonym of \"generous\" is \"mean\", and learning words in opposite pairs makes them easier to remember.","t":"「generous」的反義字是「mean」，而以相反詞成對學習單字會讓它們更容易記住。"},{"w":"homophone","p":"n.","d":"a word that sounds like another but has a different meaning","c":"同音異義字","s":"\"Their\" and \"there\" are homophone, so even native speakers sometimes mix them up when they type quickly.","t":"「their」和「there」是同音異義字，所以即使是母語人士快速打字時有時也會搞混。"},{"w":"homonym","p":"n.","d":"a word spelled and said the same as another but with a different meaning","c":"同形同音異義字","s":"\"Bat\" is a homonym, because it can mean an animal that flies at night or the stick used in baseball.","t":"「bat」是一個同形同音異義字，因為它可以指晚上飛的動物，也可以指棒球用的球棒。"},{"w":"idiom","p":"n.","d":"a group of words whose meaning is different from the single words","c":"慣用語；成語","s":"\"It's raining cats and dogs\" is a famous idiom, but you will never see real animals falling from the sky.","t":"「It's raining cats and dogs」是一個很有名的慣用語，但你永遠不會看到真的動物從天上掉下來。"},{"w":"idiomatic","p":"adj.","d":"natural and typical of native speakers","c":"道地的；慣用的","s":"Watching TV series helped Kevin learn idiomatic English, so his speaking now sounds much less like a textbook.","t":"看影集幫助凱文學到道地的英文，所以他現在說話聽起來不那麼像課本了。"},{"w":"proverb","p":"n.","d":"a short well-known saying that gives advice","c":"諺語","s":"My grandmother often quotes the proverb \"Slow and steady wins the race\", because she wants me to study a little every day.","t":"我奶奶常常引用諺語「慢而穩者勝」，因為她希望我每天讀一點書。"},{"w":"collocation","p":"n.","d":"words that are often used together","c":"搭配詞","s":"We say \"make a mistake\" but not \"do a mistake\", and learning each common collocation makes your English sound natural.","t":"我們說「make a mistake」而不是「do a mistake」，而學會每個常見的搭配詞會讓你的英文聽起來很自然。"},{"w":"phrasal verb","p":"n.phr.","d":"a verb plus a small word like \"up\" or \"off\"","c":"片語動詞","s":"\"Give up\" is a common phrasal verb, and it means to stop trying, which is very different from \"give\".","t":"「give up」是一個常見的片語動詞，意思是放棄嘗試，這和「give」的意思非常不同。"},{"w":"denotation","p":"n.","d":"the basic dictionary meaning of a word","c":"字面意義；本義","s":"The denotation of \"home\" is simply a place where you live, but the word also makes many people think of warmth and family.","t":"「home」的本義只是你居住的地方，但這個字也讓許多人聯想到溫暖和家庭。"},{"w":"literally","p":"adv.","d":"in the exact, basic meaning of the words","c":"照字面地；真正地","s":"The German word \"Handschuh\" literally means \"hand shoe\", and that is why many learners find it funny.","t":"德文字「Handschuh」照字面意思是「手鞋」，這就是許多學習者覺得它很好笑的原因。"},{"w":"definition","p":"n.","d":"a statement that explains what a word means","c":"定義","s":"I could not understand the definition in my English dictionary, so I looked at the example sentence instead, and it was much clearer.","t":"我看不懂英文字典裡的定義，所以我改看例句，結果清楚多了。"},{"w":"informal","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and used with friends, not in official situations","c":"非正式的","s":"\"Hey, what's up?\" is fine in informal chats with friends, but you should not use it in an email to your teacher.","t":"「Hey, what's up?」在和朋友非正式的聊天中沒問題，但你不應該在寫給老師的電子郵件中使用它。"},{"w":"loanword","p":"n.","d":"a word taken from another language","c":"外來語；借詞","s":"\"Sushi\" is a loanword from Japanese, and English has also borrowed words like \"tea\" from Chinese.","t":"「sushi」是來自日文的外來語，而英文也從中文借了像「tea」這樣的字。"},{"w":"neologism","p":"n.","d":"a newly invented word","c":"新造詞","s":"\"Selfie\" was once a neologism, but it became so popular that it was added to major dictionaries in just a few years.","t":"「selfie」曾經是一個新造詞，但它變得非常流行，所以短短幾年內就被收入主要字典。"},{"w":"etymology","p":"n.","d":"the history and origin of a word","c":"字源；詞源","s":"I love reading about etymology, because finding out that \"salary\" comes from the Latin word for salt is really fun.","t":"我喜歡閱讀關於字源的東西，因為發現「salary」來自拉丁文的「鹽」真的很有趣。"},{"w":"abbreviation","p":"n.","d":"a short form of a word or phrase","c":"縮寫","s":"\"Dr\" is an abbreviation of \"Doctor\", and you will see many short forms like this on signs and forms.","t":"「Dr」是「Doctor」的縮寫，而你會在標誌和表格上看到許多像這樣的簡短形式。"},{"w":"spelling","p":"n.","d":"the way letters form a word","c":"拼字","s":"English spelling can be very confusing, because \"though\", \"through\" and \"tough\" all look similar but sound different.","t":"英文拼字可能非常令人困惑，因為「though」、「through」和「tough」看起來很像，但發音不同。"},{"w":"misspell","p":"v.","d":"to spell a word wrongly","c":"拼錯","s":"I misspell my teacher's name on the birthday card, so I felt embarrassed and wrote her a new one.","t":"我在生日卡上拼錯了老師的名字，所以我覺得很尷尬，又重新寫了一張給她。"},{"w":"vocabulary","p":"n.","d":"all the words a person knows or uses","c":"字彙；詞彙量","s":"Reading for twenty minutes a day can grow your vocabulary quickly, and you will also learn how words are used in real sentences.","t":"每天閱讀二十分鐘能快速增加你的字彙，而且你也會學到單字在真實句子中如何使用。"},{"w":"word family","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of words that share the same root","c":"字族","s":"\"Decide\", \"decision\" and \"decisive\" belong to the same word family, so learning one helps you understand the others.","t":"「decide」、「decision」和「decisive」屬於同一個字族，所以學會其中一個能幫助你理解其他的。"},{"w":"profanity","p":"n.","d":"rude or offensive words","c":"髒話；粗話","s":"The film contains a lot of profanity, so the cinema did not allow children under fifteen to watch it.","t":"那部電影包含大量的髒話，所以電影院不允許十五歲以下的孩子觀看。"},{"w":"pun","p":"n.","d":"a joke that uses a word with two meanings","c":"雙關語","s":"My dad loves telling a bad pun at dinner, like \"I'm reading a book about glue, and I can't put it down.\"","t":"我爸爸喜歡在晚餐時講冷雙關語，像是「我在讀一本關於膠水的書，我放不下它。」"},{"w":"wordplay","p":"n.","d":"the clever or funny use of words","c":"文字遊戲","s":"Advertisers often use wordplay in their slogans, because a clever joke helps customers remember the product.","t":"廣告商常常在標語中使用文字遊戲，因為巧妙的玩笑能幫助顧客記住產品。"},{"w":"palindrome","p":"n.","d":"a word that reads the same backwards and forwards","c":"迴文","s":"\"Level\" is a palindrome, because you can read it from the left or from the right and it stays the same.","t":"「level」是一個迴文，因為你可以從左邊或右邊讀它，而它都保持不變。"},{"w":"onomatopoeia","p":"n.","d":"a word that copies the sound it describes","c":"擬聲詞；狀聲詞","s":"Comic books are full of onomatopoeia like \"boom\" and \"crash\", and these sound words make the action feel exciting.","t":"漫畫書裡充滿了像「boom」和「crash」這樣的狀聲詞，而這些聲音詞讓動作場面感覺很刺激。"},{"w":"simile","p":"n.","d":"a comparison using \"like\" or \"as\"","c":"明喻","s":"\"She runs like the wind\" is a simile, and writers use comparisons like this to help readers picture a scene.","t":"「她跑得像風一樣」是一個明喻，而作家用這樣的比較來幫助讀者想像畫面。"},{"w":"alliteration","p":"n.","d":"using several words that start with the same sound","c":"頭韻","s":"Many brands use alliteration, like \"Coca-Cola\" and \"PayPal\", because names with repeated sounds are easy to remember.","t":"許多品牌使用頭韻，像「Coca-Cola」和「PayPal」，因為有重複聲音的名字很容易記住。"},{"w":"oxymoron","p":"n.","d":"two words with opposite meanings used together","c":"矛盾修飾法","s":"\"Jumbo shrimp\" is a funny oxymoron, because \"jumbo\" means very big while \"shrimp\" usually means something small.","t":"「jumbo shrimp（巨無霸小蝦）」是一個有趣的矛盾修飾法，因為「jumbo」表示非常大，而「shrimp」通常表示很小的東西。"},{"w":"usage","p":"n.","d":"the way words are normally used","c":"用法","s":"The dictionary gives notes on usage, so learners can see whether a word is polite, rude, formal or old-fashioned.","t":"這本字典有關於用法的說明，所以學習者能看出一個字是禮貌的、粗魯的、正式的還是過時的。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Reading, Writing & Scripts 讀寫與文字系統","cards":[{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"a set of letters or symbols used for writing a language","c":"文字；書寫系統","s":"Korean uses a script called Hangul, and many learners can read it after only a few days of practice.","t":"韓文使用一種叫做韓文字母的文字，而許多學習者只要練習幾天就能閱讀。"},{"w":"writing system","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way a language is written down","c":"書寫系統","s":"Japanese has a complex writing system, because it mixes Chinese characters with two different sets of sound symbols.","t":"日文有一套複雜的書寫系統，因為它混合了漢字和兩套不同的表音符號。"},{"w":"Chinese character","p":"n.phr.","d":"a single written symbol used in Chinese","c":"漢字；中文字","s":"Each Chinese character has its own meaning, so foreign students must remember thousands of them before they can read a newspaper.","t":"每個中文字都有自己的意思，所以外國學生必須記住好幾千個字才能讀報紙。"},{"w":"pictograph","p":"n.","d":"a picture used as a written sign for a word","c":"象形文字","s":"The pictograph for \"mountain\" looks like three peaks, so children enjoy guessing what these old picture-words mean.","t":"代表「山」的象形文字看起來像三座山峰，所以孩子們很喜歡猜這些古老圖畫文字的意思。"},{"w":"ideogram","p":"n.","d":"a written symbol that shows an idea","c":"表意文字","s":"The no-smoking sign is a modern ideogram, because people from any country can understand it without reading a word.","t":"禁菸標誌是一種現代的表意符號，因為任何國家的人不用讀任何字就能看懂。"},{"w":"calligraphy","p":"n.","d":"the art of beautiful handwriting","c":"書法","s":"My grandfather practises Chinese calligraphy every morning, and he says that holding the brush calmly helps him relax.","t":"我爺爺每天早上練習中國書法，而他說平穩地握著毛筆能幫助他放鬆。"},{"w":"handwriting","p":"n.","d":"the way a person writes by hand","c":"筆跡；手寫字","s":"The doctor's handwriting was so messy that the pharmacist could not read it, so she called the clinic to check the medicine.","t":"那位醫生的字跡太潦草了，藥劑師看不懂，所以她打電話到診所確認藥物。"},{"w":"literate","p":"adj.","d":"able to read and write","c":"識字的","s":"Only half of the adults in the village were literate in 1950, but today almost every young person there can read and write.","t":"1950 年時那個村莊只有一半的成人識字，但如今那裡幾乎每個年輕人都能讀寫。"},{"w":"illiterate","p":"adj.","d":"unable to read or write","c":"不識字的；文盲的","s":"Her great-grandmother was illiterate because girls could not go to school then, so she asked her son to read letters for her.","t":"她的曾祖母不識字，因為當時女孩不能上學，所以她請兒子幫她讀信。"},{"w":"punctuation","p":"n.","d":"marks like commas and full stops used in writing","c":"標點符號","s":"Without correct punctuation, a sentence can be very confusing, so always check your commas before you hand in an essay.","t":"如果沒有正確的標點符號，一個句子可能會非常令人困惑，所以交作文前一定要檢查你的逗號。"},{"w":"comma","p":"n.","d":"the punctuation mark ( , )","c":"逗號","s":"\"Let's eat, Grandma\" and \"Let's eat Grandma\" mean very different things, so one small comma can save a life.","t":"「我們吃飯吧，奶奶」和「我們吃奶奶吧」意思非常不同，所以一個小小的逗號能救一條命。"},{"w":"apostrophe","p":"n.","d":"the mark ( ' ) used in words like \"it's\" or \"Tom's\"","c":"撇號","s":"Many people put an apostrophe in \"its\" by mistake, but \"it's\" only means \"it is\" or \"it has\".","t":"很多人錯誤地在「its」中加上撇號，但「it's」只表示「it is」或「it has」。"},{"w":"quotation marks","p":"n.phr.","d":"the marks (\" \") used around someone's exact words","c":"引號","s":"When you copy a sentence from a website, put it in quotation marks, or your teacher may think you are cheating.","t":"當你從網站複製一個句子時，要把它放在引號裡，否則你的老師可能會認為你在作弊。"},{"w":"hyphen","p":"n.","d":"a short line ( - ) that joins words","c":"連字號","s":"We write \"well-known\" with a hyphen when it comes before a noun, but many students forget this small rule.","t":"當「well-known」放在名詞前面時，我們要用連字號來寫，但許多學生忘了這個小規則。"},{"w":"capital letter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a big letter such as A, B or C","c":"大寫字母","s":"Every English sentence begins with a capital letter, and names of people and countries also need one.","t":"每個英文句子都以大寫字母開頭，而人名和國名也需要。"},{"w":"cursive","p":"n.","d":"handwriting where the letters are joined together","c":"草寫體","s":"Some schools no longer teach cursive, so many young people cannot read old letters written by their grandparents.","t":"有些學校不再教草寫，所以許多年輕人看不懂祖父母寫的舊信。"},{"w":"spell-checker","p":"n.","d":"a computer program that finds spelling mistakes","c":"拼字檢查程式","s":"The spell-checker did not notice that I wrote \"form\" instead of \"from\", because both are real English words.","t":"拼字檢查程式沒有發現我把「from」寫成了「form」，因為兩個都是真正的英文字。"},{"w":"autocorrect","p":"n.","d":"a phone function that changes words it thinks are wrong","c":"自動校正","s":"My phone's autocorrect changed \"meet you at five\" to \"meat you at five\", and my friend laughed at my message all day.","t":"我手機的自動校正把「五點見」改成了「五點肉你」，我朋友一整天都在笑我的訊息。"},{"w":"typo","p":"n.","d":"a small mistake in typing","c":"打字錯誤","s":"There was a typo on the restaurant menu that said \"fried lice\" instead of \"fried rice\", so many tourists took photos of it.","t":"餐廳菜單上有一個打字錯誤，把「炒飯」寫成了「炒蝨子」，所以很多觀光客都拍照留念。"},{"w":"paragraph","p":"n.","d":"a group of sentences about one main idea","c":"段落","s":"Each paragraph in your essay should start with a clear topic sentence, and the other sentences should support that idea.","t":"你文章中的每個段落都應以清楚的主題句開頭，而其他句子應該支持那個想法。"},{"w":"phonics","p":"n.","d":"a way of teaching reading through letter sounds","c":"自然發音法","s":"Young children learn phonics in their first year of school, so they can sound out new words like \"c-a-t\" by themselves.","t":"幼童在上學第一年學習自然發音法，所以他們能自己拼讀出像「c-a-t」這樣的新字。"},{"w":"romanisation","p":"n.","d":"writing a language in the Latin alphabet","c":"羅馬拼音化","s":"Street signs in Taipei use romanisation for place names, so foreign visitors can find stations even if they cannot read Chinese.","t":"台北的路標對地名使用羅馬拼音，所以外國遊客即使看不懂中文也能找到車站。"},{"w":"pinyin","p":"n.","d":"the official system for writing Chinese sounds with Roman letters","c":"漢語拼音","s":"Many foreigners learn pinyin before they learn characters, because it helps them pronounce Mandarin words correctly.","t":"許多外國人在學漢字之前先學漢語拼音，因為它能幫助他們正確發出國語字詞的音。"},{"w":"transliterate","p":"v.","d":"to write words using the letters of another alphabet","c":"音譯；轉寫","s":"Passport officers transliterate Chinese names into English letters, but the same name can be spelled in several different ways.","t":"護照官員會把中文名字音譯成英文字母，但同一個名字可能有好幾種不同的拼法。"},{"w":"scribble","p":"v.","d":"to write something quickly and carelessly","c":"潦草地寫","s":"I scribble the phone number on my hand because I had no paper, but later I could not read the last two numbers.","t":"我因為沒有紙，就把電話號碼潦草地寫在手上，但後來我看不清最後兩個數字。"},{"w":"word processor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a computer program for writing documents","c":"文書處理軟體","s":"Most students write their reports with a word processor, because it is easy to change sentences and check spelling.","t":"大多數學生用文書處理軟體寫報告，因為它很容易修改句子和檢查拼字。"},{"w":"full stop","p":"n.phr.","d":"the mark ( . ) at the end of a sentence","c":"句號","s":"Remember to put a full stop at the end of each sentence, or your reader will not know where one idea ends.","t":"記得在每個句子結尾加上句號，否則你的讀者不會知道一個想法在哪裡結束。"},{"w":"question mark","p":"n.phr.","d":"the mark ( ? ) at the end of a question","c":"問號","s":"Spanish puts an upside-down question mark at the start of a question, while English only uses one at the end.","t":"西班牙文會在問句開頭放一個倒過來的問號，而英文只在句尾用一個。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Learning & Using Languages 語言學習與使用","cards":[{"w":"foreign language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language that is not spoken in your own country","c":"外語","s":"Learning a foreign language opens many doors, because you can travel more easily and make friends from other cultures.","t":"學習一門外語能打開許多扇門，因為你可以更輕鬆地旅行，也能結交其他文化的朋友。"},{"w":"target language","p":"n.phr.","d":"the language you are learning or translating into","c":"目標語言","s":"Try to think in the target language when you speak, because translating every sentence in your head makes you slow.","t":"說話時試著用目標語言思考，因為在腦中翻譯每個句子會讓你變慢。"},{"w":"language barrier","p":"n.phr.","d":"a problem in communication caused by different languages","c":"語言障礙","s":"There was a language barrier between the doctor and the tourist, so the hospital called a volunteer who spoke Thai.","t":"醫生和那位觀光客之間存在語言障礙，所以醫院找來一位會說泰語的志工。"},{"w":"language exchange","p":"n.phr.","d":"meeting someone to practise each other's languages","c":"語言交換","s":"I joined a language exchange with a student from Spain, so I teach her Chinese for an hour and she teaches me Spanish.","t":"我和一位來自西班牙的學生參加了語言交換，所以我教她一小時中文，她教我西班牙文。"},{"w":"polyglot","p":"n.","d":"a person who can speak many languages","c":"通曉多種語言的人","s":"My uncle is a polyglot who speaks seven languages, and he says the secret is to practise a little every single day.","t":"我叔叔是一位會說七種語言的多語者，而他說祕訣就是每天練習一點點。"},{"w":"trilingual","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak three languages","c":"會說三種語言的","s":"Children in Singapore often grow up trilingual, because they speak English at school and other languages with their families.","t":"新加坡的孩子常常在三語環境中長大，因為他們在學校說英文，和家人說其他語言。"},{"w":"converse","p":"v.","d":"to have a conversation","c":"交談","s":"After a year in Tokyo, Ben could converse easily with shop owners, although he still found business meetings difficult.","t":"在東京待了一年後，班已經能輕鬆地和店主交談，雖然他仍覺得商務會議很困難。"},{"w":"chat","p":"v.","d":"to talk in a friendly, informal way","c":"聊天","s":"We chat with the hotel staff every morning, so by the end of the trip our Italian had improved a lot.","t":"我們每天早上都和飯店員工聊天，所以到旅行結束時，我們的義大利文進步了很多。"},{"w":"language learner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is studying a language","c":"語言學習者","s":"Every language learner makes mistakes, so don't be afraid to speak, because mistakes show you what to practise next.","t":"每個語言學習者都會犯錯，所以不要害怕開口，因為錯誤會告訴你接下來該練習什麼。"},{"w":"speaking test","p":"n.phr.","d":"an exam where you talk to an examiner","c":"口說測驗","s":"I felt nervous before the IELTS speaking test, but the examiner smiled and asked easy questions about my hometown first.","t":"在雅思口說測驗前我很緊張，但考官面帶微笑，先問了一些關於我家鄉的簡單問題。"},{"w":"listening comprehension","p":"n.phr.","d":"understanding what you hear","c":"聽力理解","s":"Watching the news in English improved my listening comprehension, and now I can follow lectures without reading the subtitles.","t":"看英文新聞提升了我的聽力理解，現在我不看字幕也能聽懂講座。"},{"w":"conversational","p":"adj.","d":"suitable for everyday talking","c":"會話的；日常交談的","s":"She only has conversational Japanese, so she can order food and ask for directions, but she cannot read business documents.","t":"她只會日常會話程度的日文，所以她能點餐和問路，但看不懂商業文件。"},{"w":"self-correct","p":"v.","d":"to notice and fix your own mistakes","c":"自我修正","s":"Good speakers often self-correct in the middle of a sentence, and examiners see this as a sign of strong language awareness.","t":"好的說話者常常在句子說到一半時自我修正，而考官把這看作語言意識強的跡象。"},{"w":"native-like","p":"adj.","d":"very close to the way a native speaker talks","c":"接近母語的","s":"Her pronunciation is almost native-like, so most people think she grew up in London, even though she was born in Tainan.","t":"她的發音幾乎像母語人士一樣，所以大多數人以為她在倫敦長大，即使她出生在台南。"},{"w":"shadowing","p":"n.","d":"repeating what a speaker says right after hearing it","c":"跟讀法","s":"My tutor suggested shadowing to improve my speaking, so I repeat each line of a podcast a second after I hear it.","t":"我的家教建議用跟讀法來提升口說，所以我會在聽到播客的每一句後一秒就跟著複述。"},{"w":"expat","p":"n.","d":"a person living in a foreign country","c":"旅居海外者；外籍人士","s":"As an expat in Taipei, Mark took Chinese lessons, because he wanted to talk with his neighbours and not only with foreigners.","t":"身為在台北的外籍人士，馬克上了中文課，因為他想和鄰居交談，而不只是和外國人說話。"},{"w":"verbalise","p":"v.","d":"to express ideas or feelings in words","c":"用言語表達","s":"Young children often cry when they are upset, because they cannot verbalise their feelings clearly yet.","t":"幼兒難過時常常哭，因為他們還無法清楚地用言語表達自己的感受。"},{"w":"interlocutor","p":"n.","d":"a person you are talking with","c":"對話者","s":"In the speaking exam you should look at your interlocutor and respond to their questions, rather than reciting a memorised speech.","t":"在口說考試中，你應該看著你的對話者並回應他們的問題，而不是背誦事先記好的講稿。"},{"w":"greeting","p":"n.","d":"words you say when you meet someone","c":"問候語；打招呼","s":"In Japan a bow is a common greeting, but in many Western countries people usually shake hands or wave.","t":"在日本，鞠躬是常見的打招呼方式，但在許多西方國家，人們通常握手或揮手。"},{"w":"farewell","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying goodbye","c":"告別；道別","s":"We said our farewell at the airport, and my host family gave me a card written in English and Chinese.","t":"我們在機場道別，而我的寄宿家庭送了我一張用英文和中文寫的卡片。"},{"w":"politeness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of behaving and speaking with respect","c":"禮貌","s":"In English, politeness often means adding \"could you\" or \"please\", so \"Give me water\" may sound rude to a waiter.","t":"在英文中，禮貌常常意味著加上「could you」或「please」，所以對服務生說「給我水」聽起來可能很無禮。"},{"w":"honorific","p":"n.","d":"a word or title that shows respect","c":"敬語；尊稱","s":"Korean has a special honorific ending for older people, so young learners must think carefully about who they are talking to.","t":"韓文對長輩有特別的敬語字尾，所以年輕的學習者必須仔細想想自己在跟誰說話。"},{"w":"formality","p":"n.","d":"the level of politeness and seriousness in language","c":"正式程度","s":"The formality of your email should match the reader, so you write \"Dear Professor Lin\" but \"Hi Amy\" to a friend.","t":"你電子郵件的正式程度應該配合讀者，所以你會寫「親愛的林教授」，但寫給朋友就寫「嗨，艾咪」。"},{"w":"language partner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person you practise a language with","c":"語伴","s":"My language partner lives in Canada, so we video chat every Sunday, and she corrects my grammar very kindly.","t":"我的語伴住在加拿大，所以我們每週日視訊聊天，而她會很親切地糾正我的文法。"},{"w":"language skills","p":"n.phr.","d":"abilities in listening, speaking, reading and writing","c":"語言能力","s":"Employers value strong language skills, so people who can write clear English emails often get better jobs.","t":"雇主重視良好的語言能力，所以能寫清楚英文電子郵件的人常常找到更好的工作。"},{"w":"phrasebook","p":"n.","d":"a small book of useful phrases for travellers","c":"常用語手冊","s":"We carried a Thai phrasebook on our trip, but most of the time we used hand signals and smiles instead.","t":"我們旅行時帶了一本泰語常用語手冊，但大多數時候我們還是用手勢和微笑溝通。"},{"w":"language course","p":"n.phr.","d":"a series of lessons to learn a language","c":"語言課程","s":"She took a six-week language course in Seoul last summer, and she can now read menus and chat with taxi drivers.","t":"她去年夏天在首爾上了六週的語言課程，現在她能看懂菜單，也能和計程車司機聊天。"},{"w":"crash course","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short, fast course that teaches the basics","c":"速成課程","s":"Before his business trip to Germany, my dad took a crash course in German, but he still needed an app in meetings.","t":"在去德國出差之前，我爸爸上了一個德文速成課程，但他在會議中仍需要用應用程式。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Translation & Interpreting 翻譯與口譯","cards":[{"w":"translator","p":"n.","d":"a person who changes written text into another language","c":"譯者；翻譯者","s":"The translator spent two years on the Harry Potter books, because she wanted every joke and name to work in Chinese.","t":"這位譯者花了兩年翻譯哈利波特系列，因為她希望每個笑話和名字在中文裡都行得通。"},{"w":"translation","p":"n.","d":"text or speech changed into another language","c":"翻譯；譯文","s":"I read the novel in English and then in translation, and I noticed that some funny lines lost their humour.","t":"我先讀了這本小說的英文版，接著讀了譯本，而我注意到有些好笑的句子失去了幽默感。"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n.","d":"a person who changes spoken words into another language","c":"口譯員","s":"The president spoke in French, so an interpreter stood beside him and repeated everything in English for the audience.","t":"總統用法文演講，所以一位口譯員站在他身旁，為觀眾把所有內容用英文重述一遍。"},{"w":"source language","p":"n.phr.","d":"the language that you translate from","c":"來源語言","s":"When I translate a menu, Chinese is the source language, and English is the language I translate into.","t":"當我翻譯菜單時，中文是來源語言，而英文是我翻譯成的語言。"},{"w":"source text","p":"n.phr.","d":"the original text that is being translated","c":"原文","s":"A good translator reads the whole source text first, because the meaning of the beginning may depend on the ending.","t":"好的譯者會先讀完整篇原文，因為開頭的意思可能取決於結尾。"},{"w":"mistranslate","p":"v.","d":"to translate something wrongly","c":"誤譯；翻錯","s":"The sign mistranslate \"slippery floor\" as \"carefully slide\", so tourists took funny photos, but nobody understood the warning.","t":"那個標誌把「地板濕滑」翻錯成「小心地滑」，所以觀光客拍了好笑的照片，但沒人看懂這個警告。"},{"w":"machine translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"translation done by a computer","c":"機器翻譯","s":"machine translation is fast and free, but it can still make strange mistakes with idioms and jokes.","t":"機器翻譯又快又免費，但它在慣用語和笑話上仍可能犯奇怪的錯誤。"},{"w":"simultaneous interpreting","p":"n.phr.","d":"interpreting while the speaker is still talking","c":"同步口譯","s":"simultaneous interpreting is very tiring, so interpreters at the United Nations usually change places every thirty minutes.","t":"同步口譯非常累人，所以聯合國的口譯員通常每三十分鐘換一次班。"},{"w":"consecutive interpreting","p":"n.phr.","d":"interpreting after the speaker stops for a moment","c":"逐步口譯","s":"In consecutive interpreting the speaker pauses after a few sentences, and then the interpreter repeats the message in the other language.","t":"在逐步口譯中，講者說幾句後會停頓，然後口譯員用另一種語言重述訊息。"},{"w":"dub","p":"v.","d":"to replace the voices in a film with another language","c":"配音","s":"Many cartoons are dub into Mandarin for young children, because they cannot read subtitles fast enough.","t":"許多卡通會配上國語給幼兒看，因為他們讀字幕的速度不夠快。"},{"w":"localise","p":"v.","d":"to change a product to suit a local market and language","c":"在地化","s":"The company had to localise its game for Taiwan, so it changed the jokes and added local foods to the story.","t":"這家公司必須為台灣把遊戲在地化，所以它改了笑話，並在故事中加入了當地食物。"},{"w":"subtitling","p":"n.","d":"the work of adding translated words at the bottom of a screen","c":"字幕翻譯","s":"subtitling is harder than it looks, because translators must fit each line into the screen while people are still speaking.","t":"字幕翻譯比看起來難，因為譯者必須在人物仍在說話時把每一行塞進螢幕裡。"},{"w":"literal translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"a translation that follows the words exactly","c":"直譯","s":"A literal translation of \"break a leg\" sounds terrible in Chinese, but the phrase actually means \"good luck\" to actors.","t":"「break a leg」的直譯在中文裡聽起來很可怕，但這個片語對演員來說其實是「祝好運」的意思。"},{"w":"free translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"a translation that keeps the meaning but changes the words","c":"意譯","s":"The poet chose a free translation, because keeping the rhyme and feeling was more important to her than copying every word.","t":"這位詩人選擇了意譯，因為對她來說保留押韻和情感比照抄每個字更重要。"},{"w":"back-translation","p":"n.","d":"translating a text back into its first language to check it","c":"回譯","s":"The medical team used back-translation to check the survey, so a second translator turned the Chinese version back into English.","t":"醫療團隊用回譯來檢查問卷，所以由第二位譯者把中文版翻回英文。"},{"w":"faithful","p":"adj.","d":"keeping close to the original meaning","c":"忠實的","s":"Her translation is faithful to the original novel, but it also reads naturally, which is why it won an award.","t":"她的譯文忠於原著小說，但讀起來也很自然，這就是它得獎的原因。"},{"w":"untranslatable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to translate exactly","c":"無法翻譯的","s":"The Danish word \"hygge\" is often called untranslatable, because no single English word captures that cosy, happy feeling.","t":"丹麥字「hygge」常被稱為無法翻譯的，因為沒有一個英文字能抓住那種溫馨、快樂的感覺。"},{"w":"gloss","p":"n.","d":"a short explanation of a difficult word in a text","c":"注釋；註解","s":"The textbook gives a Chinese gloss beside each difficult word, so students can keep reading without opening a dictionary.","t":"課本在每個難字旁邊都附上中文註解，所以學生不用翻字典就能繼續讀下去。"},{"w":"footnote","p":"n.","d":"a note at the bottom of a page","c":"註腳","s":"The translator added a footnote to explain the Chinese joke, because English readers would not understand it otherwise.","t":"譯者加了一個註腳來解釋這個中文笑話，因為否則英文讀者不會懂。"},{"w":"interpreter booth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small soundproof room where interpreters work","c":"口譯廂","s":"The two interpreters sat in a glass interpreter booth at the back of the hall, and they could see every speaker clearly.","t":"兩位口譯員坐在大廳後方的玻璃口譯廂裡，而他們能清楚看到每位講者。"},{"w":"earpiece","p":"n.","d":"a small device worn in the ear to hear sound","c":"耳機","s":"Each delegate wore an earpiece during the meeting, so they could hear the speech in their own language.","t":"每位代表在會議中都戴著耳機，所以他們能聽到用自己語言播出的演講。"},{"w":"sight translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"reading a document in one language aloud in another","c":"視譯","s":"The court interpreter did a sight translation of the letter, so she read the Vietnamese text aloud in Chinese for the judge.","t":"法庭口譯員對那封信做了視譯，所以她把越南文內容直接用中文唸給法官聽。"},{"w":"court interpreter","p":"n.phr.","d":"an interpreter who works in courtrooms","c":"法庭口譯員","s":"The court interpreter must translate every word exactly, because a small mistake could change the result of a trial.","t":"法庭口譯員必須精確翻譯每一個字，因為一個小錯誤就可能改變審判的結果。"},{"w":"speech-to-text","p":"adj.","d":"changing spoken words into written words automatically","c":"語音轉文字的","s":"The teacher uses a speech-to-text app in class, so deaf students can read her words on their tablets as she speaks.","t":"老師在課堂上使用語音轉文字的應用程式，所以聽障學生能在她說話時從平板上讀到她的話。"},{"w":"translation app","p":"n.phr.","d":"a phone program that translates words or speech","c":"翻譯應用程式","s":"We used a translation app to read the menu in Seoul, but it translated one dish as \"angry chicken\", which made us laugh.","t":"我們在首爾用翻譯應用程式看菜單，但它把一道菜翻成「生氣的雞」，讓我們笑了出來。"},{"w":"neural machine translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"computer translation that uses AI networks to learn from data","c":"神經機器翻譯","s":"neural machine translation produces smoother sentences than older systems, because it looks at whole sentences instead of single words.","t":"神經機器翻譯產生的句子比舊系統更流暢，因為它看的是整個句子而不是單一的字。"},{"w":"post-editing","p":"n.","d":"fixing a machine translation by a human","c":"譯後編輯","s":"Many translators now do post-editing, so they check and correct AI translations instead of starting from a blank page.","t":"許多譯者現在做譯後編輯，所以他們檢查和修正 AI 的翻譯，而不是從一張白紙開始。"},{"w":"language pair","p":"n.phr.","d":"the two languages a translator works between","c":"語言對","s":"Her main language pair is Japanese to Chinese, but she also accepts some simple English projects.","t":"她主要的語言對是日譯中，但她也接一些簡單的英文案子。"},{"w":"voice-over","p":"n.","d":"a voice heard in a film or video without seeing the speaker","c":"旁白；畫外音","s":"The documentary had a Chinese voice-over, so we could understand the story while we watched the animals in Africa.","t":"這部紀錄片有中文旁白，所以我們能一邊看非洲的動物，一邊了解故事內容。"},{"w":"speech translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"technology that translates spoken language aloud","c":"語音翻譯","s":"New earbuds offer instant speech translation, so two travellers can talk to each other even if they share no language.","t":"新型耳機提供即時語音翻譯，所以即使兩位旅客沒有共通語言，也能彼此交談。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"World Languages & Language Change 世界語言與語言變遷","cards":[{"w":"language family","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of languages that come from one older language","c":"語系","s":"English and Hindi belong to the same language family, although speakers of the two languages cannot understand each other today.","t":"英文和印地文屬於同一個語系，雖然兩種語言的使用者如今無法聽懂彼此。"},{"w":"lingua franca","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shared language used by people with different first languages","c":"通用語","s":"English has become a lingua franca in international business, so a Japanese manager and a Brazilian client may talk in English.","t":"英文已成為國際商務的通用語，所以一位日本經理和一位巴西客戶可能會用英文交談。"},{"w":"official language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language used by a government and in law","c":"官方語言","s":"Canada has two official language, so road signs and food labels there use both English and French.","t":"加拿大有兩種官方語言，所以那裡的路標和食品標籤同時使用英文和法文。"},{"w":"minority language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language spoken by a small part of a population","c":"少數語言","s":"Welsh is a minority language in the UK, but children can now study all their subjects in Welsh at many schools.","t":"威爾斯語在英國是一種少數語言，但現在許多學校的孩子可以用威爾斯語學習所有科目。"},{"w":"endangered language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language that may soon have no speakers","c":"瀕危語言","s":"An endangered language often has only older speakers, because young people move to cities and use the national language instead.","t":"瀕危語言常常只剩年長的使用者，因為年輕人搬到城市並改用國家語言。"},{"w":"language death","p":"n.phr.","d":"when the last speakers of a language die out","c":"語言消亡","s":"language death is happening faster than ever, and experts believe half of the world's languages may disappear this century.","t":"語言消亡正以前所未有的速度發生，而專家認為世界上一半的語言可能會在本世紀消失。"},{"w":"language revival","p":"n.phr.","d":"efforts to bring a disappearing language back into use","c":"語言復振","s":"Hebrew is the most famous language revival story, because it became an everyday language again after many centuries.","t":"希伯來文是最有名的語言復振故事，因為它在許多世紀後再次成為日常語言。"},{"w":"creole","p":"n.","d":"a language that grew from mixing two languages and became a first language","c":"克里奧爾語；混合語","s":"In Haiti most people speak a French-based creole, and children learn it at home as their first language.","t":"在海地，大多數人說一種以法文為基礎的克里奧爾語，而孩子們在家把它當作第一語言學習。"},{"w":"pidgin","p":"n.","d":"a simple mixed language used for trade between groups","c":"洋涇濱語；混雜語","s":"Sailors and traders once used a simple pidgin to do business, although nobody spoke it as their mother tongue.","t":"水手和商人曾經用一種簡單的混雜語做生意，雖然沒有人把它當作母語。"},{"w":"language contact","p":"n.phr.","d":"when speakers of different languages meet and influence each other","c":"語言接觸","s":"Taiwanese Mandarin has many Japanese and Hokkien words because of language contact, and these words are now part of daily life.","t":"由於語言接觸，台灣華語有許多日語和閩南語詞彙，而這些詞如今已成為日常生活的一部分。"},{"w":"global English","p":"n.phr.","d":"English used around the world as an international language","c":"全球英語","s":"Teachers who promote global English say that clear communication matters more than sounding British or American.","t":"推廣全球英語的老師說，清楚溝通比聽起來像英國人或美國人更重要。"},{"w":"World Englishes","p":"n.phr.","d":"the different kinds of English used in different countries","c":"世界英語變體","s":"Singapore, India and Nigeria all have their own World Englishes, and each variety has special words and accents.","t":"新加坡、印度和奈及利亞都有自己的世界英語變體，而每一種都有特別的詞彙和口音。"},{"w":"calque","p":"n.","d":"a phrase translated word by word from another language","c":"仿譯詞","s":"\"Long time no see\" may be a calque from Chinese, because it follows the Chinese word order rather than normal English grammar.","t":"「Long time no see」可能是來自中文的仿譯詞，因為它遵循中文的詞序，而不是一般的英文文法。"},{"w":"language shift","p":"n.phr.","d":"when a community stops using one language and uses another","c":"語言轉移","s":"In many immigrant families a language shift happens within three generations, so the grandchildren speak only the new country's language.","t":"在許多移民家庭中，語言轉移在三代之內就會發生，所以孫子輩只會說新國家的語言。"},{"w":"last speaker","p":"n.phr.","d":"the final living person who speaks a language","c":"最後的使用者","s":"When the last speaker of a language dies, many old songs and stories can disappear unless someone records them first.","t":"當一種語言的最後一位使用者去世時，許多古老的歌曲和故事可能就此消失，除非有人先把它們錄下來。"},{"w":"oral tradition","p":"n.phr.","d":"stories and knowledge passed on by speaking, not writing","c":"口述傳統","s":"The tribe had no written language, but its oral tradition kept their history alive, because elders told the stories again and again.","t":"這個部落沒有文字，但他們的口述傳統讓歷史延續下來，因為長老們一再地講述那些故事。"},{"w":"linguistic diversity","p":"n.phr.","d":"the variety of different languages in a place","c":"語言多樣性","s":"Papua New Guinea has amazing linguistic diversity, because more than 800 languages are spoken there by fewer than ten million people.","t":"巴布亞紐幾內亞擁有驚人的語言多樣性，因為不到一千萬人在那裡使用超過八百種語言。"},{"w":"language policy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a government's rules about which languages are used","c":"語言政策","s":"The new language policy requires schools to teach a local language, so every pupil now has at least one hour of it each week.","t":"新的語言政策要求學校教授一種本土語言，所以每位學生現在每週至少有一小時這門課。"},{"w":"mother-tongue education","p":"n.phr.","d":"teaching children in their first language","c":"母語教育","s":"Research supports mother-tongue education in the early years, because children learn to read faster in a language they already speak.","t":"研究支持在早年實施母語教育，因為孩子用他們已經會說的語言學習閱讀會更快。"},{"w":"proto-language","p":"n.","d":"an ancient language that later languages developed from","c":"原始語","s":"Linguists have rebuilt many words of the proto-language behind European languages, even though nobody ever wrote it down.","t":"語言學家已經重建了歐洲語言背後那個原始語的許多字詞，即使從來沒有人把它寫下來。"},{"w":"Esperanto","p":"n.","d":"an invented language created to be easy for everyone","c":"世界語","s":"Esperanto was invented in 1887 to help people from different countries communicate, and today a few thousand families still speak it at home.","t":"世界語於 1887 年被發明出來，以幫助不同國家的人溝通，而如今仍有幾千個家庭在家中使用它。"},{"w":"constructed language","p":"n.phr.","d":"a language that someone designed on purpose","c":"人造語言","s":"Klingon is a constructed language from Star Trek, but some fans have learned it so well that they can hold whole conversations.","t":"克林貢語是來自《星艦迷航記》的人造語言，但有些粉絲學得非常好，能進行完整的對話。"},{"w":"speech community","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of people who share a language or way of speaking","c":"言語社群","s":"Gamers form their own speech community online, so outsiders often cannot understand their fast messages full of special terms.","t":"玩家在網路上形成自己的言語社群，所以外人常常看不懂他們充滿專門術語的快速訊息。"},{"w":"language planning","p":"n.phr.","d":"deliberate efforts to manage how languages are used","c":"語言規劃","s":"After independence the country needed careful language planning, because people spoke more than twenty languages and needed one for schools.","t":"獨立後這個國家需要謹慎的語言規劃，因為人們說二十多種語言，而學校需要一種共同語言。"},{"w":"vernacular","p":"n.","d":"the everyday language spoken by ordinary people","c":"日常用語；方言白話","s":"The priest began to preach in the vernacular instead of Latin, so ordinary villagers could finally understand his message.","t":"那位神父開始用白話而非拉丁文佈道，所以一般村民終於能聽懂他的訊息。"},{"w":"language rights","p":"n.phr.","d":"people's right to use their own language","c":"語言權","s":"Indigenous groups are fighting for language rights, so they can use their own languages in courts, hospitals and schools.","t":"原住民族群正在爭取語言權，以便他們能在法院、醫院和學校使用自己的語言。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (accessibility – eulogy)","cards":[{"w":"accessibility","p":"n.","d":"how easy something is to reach, use or understand","c":"可及性；易用性","s":"The museum improved the accessibility of its website, so blind visitors can now listen to every page with a screen reader.","t":"博物館改善了網站的易用性，所以視障訪客現在能用螢幕閱讀器聆聽每一頁。"},{"w":"advocacy","p":"n.","d":"public support for an idea or group","c":"倡議；提倡","s":"Her advocacy for sign language helped deaf students, because the school finally hired two interpreters for its classes.","t":"她對手語的倡議幫助了聽障學生，因為學校終於為課堂聘請了兩位口譯員。"},{"w":"allocation","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something given for a purpose","c":"分配；配額","s":"The school's budget allocation for language classes was cut, so the French club had to buy its own books.","t":"學校給語言課程的預算分配被刪減了，所以法文社必須自己買書。"},{"w":"amendment","p":"n.","d":"a small change made to a law or document","c":"修正案；修訂","s":"Parliament passed an amendment to the education law, and now every primary school must offer a local language.","t":"國會通過了教育法的修正案，現在每所小學都必須開設一種本土語言課程。"},{"w":"appendix","p":"n.","d":"extra information at the end of a book or report","c":"附錄","s":"The grammar book has a useful appendix of irregular verbs, so I check it whenever I am not sure about a past tense.","t":"這本文法書有一份實用的不規則動詞附錄，所以每當我不確定過去式時就會查看它。"},{"w":"appreciation","p":"n.","d":"understanding and enjoying the value of something","c":"欣賞；體會","s":"Learning Japanese gave me a deeper appreciation of anime, because I could finally catch the jokes that subtitles missed.","t":"學日文讓我對動漫有更深的體會，因為我終於能聽懂字幕漏掉的笑話。"},{"w":"assurance","p":"n.","d":"a promise that makes someone feel confident","c":"保證；擔保","s":"The company gave customers an assurance that every translation would be checked twice, so many hospitals chose its service.","t":"這家公司向客戶保證每份翻譯都會檢查兩次，所以許多醫院選擇了它的服務。"},{"w":"attribution","p":"n.","d":"saying who wrote or created something","c":"出處標明；歸屬","s":"You must give clear attribution when you use a quote from a book, or your essay may be marked as plagiarised.","t":"當你引用書中的句子時必須清楚標明出處，否則你的文章可能被判定為抄襲。"},{"w":"allegory","p":"n.","d":"a story with a hidden moral or political meaning","c":"寓言；諷喻","s":"Animal Farm looks like a story about pigs, but it is really an allegory about power, and students discuss it in class.","t":"《動物農莊》看似一個關於豬的故事，但它其實是一則關於權力的寓言，學生們會在課堂上討論它。"},{"w":"allusion","p":"n.","d":"an indirect mention of something","c":"暗指；典故","s":"The speech contained an allusion to a famous Chinese poem, so the foreign guests needed the interpreter to explain it.","t":"演講中包含了一個著名中國詩詞的典故，所以外國賓客需要口譯員解釋。"},{"w":"anachronism","p":"n.","d":"something placed in the wrong historical time","c":"時代錯置","s":"The film about ancient Rome had an anachronism in one scene, because a soldier was clearly wearing a wristwatch.","t":"那部關於古羅馬的電影在某個場景中有時代錯置的錯誤，因為一名士兵明顯戴著手錶。"},{"w":"anecdote","p":"n.","d":"a short interesting story about a real event","c":"軼事；小故事","s":"The professor began with a funny anecdote about getting lost in Paris, and everyone relaxed before the serious lecture.","t":"教授以一個在巴黎迷路的好笑小故事開場，而大家在嚴肅的講座開始前都放鬆了。"},{"w":"antithesis","p":"n.","d":"the exact opposite","c":"正好相反；對立面","s":"His careless speaking style is the antithesis of his sister's, because she plans every word before she opens her mouth.","t":"他隨便的說話風格和他姊姊的正好相反，因為她開口前會規劃好每個字。"},{"w":"approbation","p":"n.","d":"approval or praise","c":"讚許；認可","s":"The young translator won the approbation of the famous author, so her name now appears on the cover of the new edition.","t":"這位年輕譯者贏得了知名作家的讚許，所以她的名字現在出現在新版的封面上。"},{"w":"arbiter","p":"n.","d":"a person who judges what is right or correct","c":"仲裁者；權威裁定者","s":"Many people treat the Oxford dictionary as the final arbiter of correct English, but language keeps changing anyway.","t":"許多人把牛津字典當作正確英文的最終裁定者，但語言無論如何都在不斷變化。"},{"w":"assent","p":"n.","d":"agreement or approval","c":"同意；贊成","s":"The teacher nodded her assent, so we started recording our English podcast during the lunch break.","t":"老師點頭表示同意，所以我們在午休時間開始錄製英文播客。"},{"w":"candour","p":"n.","d":"honest and open speech","c":"坦率；直言","s":"I appreciated my tutor's candour about my accent, because she told me exactly which sounds I needed to fix.","t":"我很感謝家教對我口音的坦率，因為她準確告訴我哪些音需要改正。"},{"w":"catharsis","p":"n.","d":"a release of strong emotions that makes you feel better","c":"情緒宣洩；淨化","s":"Writing a diary in English was a kind of catharsis for her, because she could express feelings she could not say aloud.","t":"用英文寫日記對她來說是一種情緒宣洩，因為她能表達說不出口的感受。"},{"w":"circumlocution","p":"n.","d":"using many words when a few would do","c":"拐彎抹角；迂迴說法","s":"When you forget a word, circumlocution can help you, so you might say \"the thing that opens doors\" instead of \"key\".","t":"當你忘記一個字時，迂迴說法能幫助你，所以你可以說「開門的東西」而不是「鑰匙」。"},{"w":"compendium","p":"n.","d":"a book with a lot of information on one subject","c":"彙編；概要","s":"My uncle gave me a compendium of English idioms, and I read a few pages on the bus every morning.","t":"我叔叔送我一本英文慣用語彙編，而我每天早上在公車上讀幾頁。"},{"w":"decorum","p":"n.","d":"polite and correct behaviour","c":"禮節；端莊得體","s":"The students behaved with great decorum during the ceremony, but they started shouting and laughing as soon as it ended.","t":"學生們在典禮中表現得非常得體，但典禮一結束他們就開始大叫大笑。"},{"w":"disdain","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that something is not worth respect","c":"鄙視；輕蔑","s":"Some people show disdain for text-message slang, but linguists see it as a creative new way of writing.","t":"有些人對簡訊俚語表現出輕蔑，但語言學家把它看作一種有創意的新書寫方式。"},{"w":"dissonance","p":"n.","d":"a lack of agreement or harmony","c":"不和諧；不一致","s":"There was a clear dissonance between the minister's words and his actions, so voters stopped believing his promises.","t":"部長的言行之間有明顯的不一致，所以選民不再相信他的承諾。"},{"w":"duplicity","p":"n.","d":"dishonest behaviour meant to trick people","c":"欺騙；口是心非","s":"The salesman's duplicity shocked us, because he said the phone was new while he knew it had been repaired.","t":"那位推銷員的欺騙行為讓我們震驚，因為他明知手機修過卻說是全新的。"},{"w":"eulogy","p":"n.","d":"a speech praising someone who has died","c":"悼詞","s":"My cousin gave a moving eulogy at our grandfather's funeral, and she spoke in both Hakka and Mandarin.","t":"我表姊在爺爺的葬禮上發表了一篇感人的悼詞，而且她用客家話和國語兩種語言說。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (foible – banal)","cards":[{"w":"foible","p":"n.","d":"a small weakness in someone's character","c":"小缺點；怪癖","s":"Correcting everyone's grammar is my teacher's only foible, but we forgive her because she is so kind.","t":"糾正每個人的文法是我們老師唯一的小怪癖，但我們原諒她，因為她人非常好。"},{"w":"guile","p":"n.","d":"clever but dishonest behaviour","c":"狡詐；詭計","s":"The fox in the story uses guile to steal the crow's cheese, so the lesson is to be careful of people who flatter you.","t":"故事中的狐狸用詭計偷走了烏鴉的起司，所以寓意是要小心奉承你的人。"},{"w":"heresy","p":"n.","d":"an idea that strongly opposes accepted beliefs","c":"異端邪說","s":"Splitting an infinitive was once seen as heresy by grammar teachers, but most writers today think it is perfectly fine.","t":"拆開不定詞曾被文法老師視為異端，但現今大多數作家認為這完全沒問題。"},{"w":"hubris","p":"n.","d":"too much pride and self-confidence","c":"傲慢；狂妄自大","s":"The student's hubris led him to skip revision, because he believed his English was perfect, but he failed the writing test.","t":"那名學生的狂妄自大讓他略過複習，因為他相信自己的英文完美無缺，但他寫作測驗不及格。"},{"w":"iconoclast","p":"n.","d":"a person who attacks traditional ideas","c":"反傳統者；打破舊習的人","s":"The poet was an iconoclast who ignored punctuation rules, and young readers loved her daring style.","t":"這位詩人是一個反傳統的人，她無視標點符號規則，而年輕讀者喜愛她大膽的風格。"},{"w":"levity","p":"n.","d":"humour in a serious situation","c":"輕鬆幽默；輕率","s":"A little levity helped the nervous candidates, so the examiner told a short joke before the speaking test began.","t":"一點輕鬆幽默幫助了緊張的考生，所以考官在口說測驗開始前講了個小笑話。"},{"w":"maverick","p":"n.","d":"a person who thinks and acts independently","c":"特立獨行的人","s":"The new teacher was a maverick who taught grammar through rap songs, and the students' scores rose quickly.","t":"新老師是個特立獨行的人，他透過饒舌歌教文法，而學生的成績迅速提高。"},{"w":"neophyte","p":"n.","d":"a beginner","c":"新手；初學者","s":"As a neophyte in Korean, I could only say hello and thank you, but the shop owners still smiled and helped me.","t":"身為韓文初學者，我只會說你好和謝謝，但店主們還是微笑著幫助我。"},{"w":"nostalgia","p":"n.","d":"a happy but sad feeling about the past","c":"懷舊；思鄉之情","s":"Hearing her hometown dialect filled her with nostalgia, because it reminded her of summers at her grandmother's house.","t":"聽到家鄉的方言讓她充滿懷舊之情，因為那讓她想起在外婆家度過的夏天。"},{"w":"paragon","p":"n.","d":"a perfect example of a quality","c":"典範；模範","s":"Our principal is a paragon of patience, because she listens to every student calmly even when they are shouting.","t":"我們校長是耐心的典範，因為即使學生大吼大叫，她也會冷靜地聆聽每個人。"},{"w":"pariah","p":"n.","d":"a person who is rejected by others","c":"被排斥的人；棄兒","s":"After he posted rude comments online, the singer became a pariah, and many fans stopped buying his music.","t":"在網上發布無禮留言後，這位歌手成了被排斥的人，許多粉絲不再買他的音樂。"},{"w":"predilection","p":"n.","d":"a strong liking for something","c":"偏好；偏愛","s":"The author has a predilection for long sentences, so translators often have to split them into shorter ones in Chinese.","t":"這位作家偏好長句子，所以譯者常常必須在中文裡把它們拆成較短的句子。"},{"w":"probity","p":"n.","d":"complete honesty","c":"正直；誠實","s":"Interpreters must show great probity, because they hear secret information and must never share it with anyone.","t":"口譯員必須展現高度的正直，因為他們會聽到機密資訊，而且絕不能與任何人分享。"},{"w":"protagonist","p":"n.","d":"the main character in a story","c":"主角","s":"The protagonist of the novel is a young interpreter, and the story follows her life during the war.","t":"這部小說的主角是一位年輕的口譯員，而故事描寫她在戰爭期間的生活。"},{"w":"rancour","p":"n.","d":"long-lasting anger and bitterness","c":"積怨；怨恨","s":"The two writers argued for years, but there was no rancour between them, because they still respected each other's work.","t":"兩位作家爭論了好幾年，但他們之間沒有怨恨，因為他們仍然尊重彼此的作品。"},{"w":"veneer","p":"n.","d":"a thin outer appearance that hides the truth","c":"虛飾；表面","s":"Under a veneer of politeness, the letter was actually very angry, and the translator worked hard to keep that hidden tone.","t":"在禮貌的表面下，這封信其實非常憤怒，而譯者努力保留那種隱藏的語氣。"},{"w":"sycophant","p":"n.","d":"a person who praises powerful people to get advantages","c":"諂媚者；馬屁精","s":"The manager was surrounded by sycophant who agreed with every idea, so nobody warned him about the bad translation.","t":"經理身邊圍繞著什麼想法都附和的馬屁精，所以沒有人提醒他那份翻譯很糟。"},{"w":"globalisation","p":"n.","d":"the process of the world becoming more connected","c":"全球化","s":"globalisation has made English more useful, but it has also put pressure on many small local languages.","t":"全球化讓英文變得更有用，但也對許多當地的小語種造成壓力。"},{"w":"admissible","p":"adj.","d":"allowed or accepted, especially in court","c":"可被接受的；可採納的","s":"The recording was not admissible in court, because the translation had not been checked by an official interpreter.","t":"那段錄音在法庭上不可被採納，因為翻譯沒有經過官方口譯員檢查。"},{"w":"affable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and easy to talk to","c":"和藹可親的","s":"The affable shopkeeper chatted with us in slow English, so even my little brother felt brave enough to answer.","t":"那位和藹可親的店主用慢速的英文和我們聊天，所以連我弟弟都有勇氣回答。"},{"w":"amiable","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant and friendly","c":"友善的；親切的","s":"My host father was an amiable man who corrected my mistakes gently, and he never made me feel stupid.","t":"我的寄宿爸爸是個親切的人，他溫和地糾正我的錯誤，從不讓我覺得自己很笨。"},{"w":"amicable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and without arguments","c":"友好的；和睦的","s":"The two companies reached an amicable agreement, so the translation project continued without any lawyers.","t":"兩家公司達成了友好的協議，所以翻譯計畫在沒有律師介入的情況下繼續進行。"},{"w":"apposite","p":"adj.","d":"very suitable for the situation","c":"恰當的；貼切的","s":"She closed her speech with an apposite proverb, and the audience clapped because it matched the topic perfectly.","t":"她用一句貼切的諺語結束演講，觀眾都鼓掌了，因為它完美地呼應了主題。"},{"w":"authoritarian","p":"adj.","d":"demanding total obedience","c":"專制的；獨裁的","s":"The authoritarian government banned books in minority languages, but families kept teaching their children at home in secret.","t":"專制的政府禁止少數語言的書籍，但家庭們仍在家中秘密地教孩子。"},{"w":"banal","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and boring","c":"陳腐的；平淡無奇的","s":"The song's lyrics were banal, but the melody was so catchy that it became a hit anyway.","t":"這首歌的歌詞平淡無奇，但旋律非常好記，所以它還是紅了。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (bemused – impertinent)","cards":[{"w":"bemused","p":"adj.","d":"confused and puzzled","c":"困惑的","s":"The tourist looked bemused when the waiter answered in fast Taiwanese, so I explained the menu to him in English.","t":"當服務生用快速的台語回答時，那位觀光客看起來很困惑，所以我用英文為他解釋菜單。"},{"w":"bilateral","p":"adj.","d":"involving two groups or countries","c":"雙邊的","s":"The two countries signed a bilateral agreement, so students can now study the other country's language with free scholarships.","t":"兩國簽署了一項雙邊協議，所以學生現在能獲得免費獎學金去學習對方國家的語言。"},{"w":"bombastic","p":"adj.","d":"using big words to sound important","c":"浮誇的；誇大其詞的","s":"His essay was full of bombastic language, but the teacher said simple and clear words would have been much better.","t":"他的文章充滿浮誇的語言，但老師說簡單清楚的字會好得多。"},{"w":"bona fide","p":"adj.","d":"real and genuine","c":"真正的；真誠的","s":"Only bona fide students can get the discount, so you must show your student card at the language centre.","t":"只有真正的學生才能享有折扣，所以你必須在語言中心出示學生證。"},{"w":"brusque","p":"adj.","d":"short and rude in speech","c":"唐突的；粗魯簡短的","s":"The officer's brusque reply upset the tourist, but maybe he was just tired and not good at English.","t":"那位官員粗魯簡短的回答讓觀光客不高興，但也許他只是累了，而且英文不好。"},{"w":"caustic","p":"adj.","d":"very critical in a cruel way","c":"刻薄的；尖酸的","s":"The critic wrote a caustic review of the translation, but readers still loved the book and bought thousands of copies.","t":"那位評論家對譯本寫了一篇尖酸刻薄的評論，但讀者仍然喜愛這本書，買了好幾千本。"},{"w":"conciliatory","p":"adj.","d":"trying to end an argument and make peace","c":"安撫的；和解的","s":"After the argument, he sent a conciliatory message in Chinese and English, so his friend finally agreed to talk again.","t":"爭吵後，他用中英文發了一則和解的訊息，所以他朋友終於同意再談一談。"},{"w":"congruent","p":"adj.","d":"matching or in agreement with something","c":"一致的；相符的","s":"Your body language should be congruent with your words, because a smile with angry words confuses the listener.","t":"你的肢體語言應該和你說的話一致，因為帶著微笑說生氣的話會讓聽者困惑。"},{"w":"contemptuous","p":"adj.","d":"showing no respect","c":"輕視的；鄙夷的","s":"He gave a contemptuous laugh when I made a grammar mistake, so I decided to practise with a kinder partner.","t":"我犯文法錯誤時他發出輕蔑的笑聲，所以我決定和一位更友善的夥伴練習。"},{"w":"convoluted","p":"adj.","d":"very complicated and hard to follow","c":"錯綜複雜的；費解的","s":"The instructions were so convoluted that nobody could follow them, so the company rewrote them in plain English.","t":"那些說明複雜難懂到沒人能照著做，所以公司用淺白的英文重寫了。"},{"w":"credulous","p":"adj.","d":"too ready to believe things","c":"輕信的；易受騙的","s":"My credulous little sister believed that eating carrots would help her speak French, and she ate five that day.","t":"我那容易輕信的妹妹相信吃紅蘿蔔能幫助她說法文，結果她那天吃了五根。"},{"w":"deft","p":"adj.","d":"quick and skilful","c":"靈巧的；熟練的","s":"The interpreter made a deft change to the joke, so the Chinese audience laughed at exactly the right moment.","t":"口譯員對那個笑話做了巧妙的改動，所以中文觀眾在恰當的時刻笑了出來。"},{"w":"diffident","p":"adj.","d":"shy and lacking confidence","c":"缺乏自信的；羞怯的","s":"She was diffident about speaking English at first, but the friendly class helped her become one of the most active students.","t":"她一開始對說英文缺乏自信，但友善的班級幫助她成為最活躍的學生之一。"},{"w":"diminutive","p":"adj.","d":"very small","c":"極小的；矮小的","s":"The diminutive girl had a surprisingly loud voice, so she won the school speech contest without a microphone.","t":"那個嬌小的女孩有著驚人的大嗓門，所以她沒用麥克風就贏得了學校演講比賽。"},{"w":"effusive","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of feeling, especially praise","c":"熱情洋溢的；過分熱情的","s":"The author sent the translator an effusive thank-you letter, and she hung it on the wall above her desk.","t":"作家寄給譯者一封熱情洋溢的感謝信，而她把信掛在書桌上方的牆上。"},{"w":"elated","p":"adj.","d":"very happy and excited","c":"興高采烈的","s":"I was elated when I got band 7 in IELTS, so I called my parents right away and we went out for dinner.","t":"我雅思考到 7 分時欣喜若狂，所以我馬上打電話給爸媽，然後我們出去吃晚餐。"},{"w":"facetious","p":"adj.","d":"joking at the wrong time","c":"開玩笑的；不正經的","s":"His facetious comment during the serious budget meeting annoyed the boss, so he apologised to her later that afternoon.","t":"他在嚴肅的預算會議中說了一句不正經的話惹惱了老闆，所以他那天下午稍晚向她道歉了。"},{"w":"fickle","p":"adj.","d":"changing your mind often","c":"善變的","s":"Teenagers can be fickle about slang, so a word that is cool this month may sound silly next year.","t":"青少年對俚語可能很善變，所以這個月很酷的字明年可能聽起來很蠢。"},{"w":"furtive","p":"adj.","d":"secret and trying not to be noticed","c":"偷偷摸摸的","s":"The student took a furtive look at his phone dictionary, but the examiner noticed and took it away.","t":"那名學生偷偷摸摸地看了一眼手機字典，但考官注意到並把它拿走了。"},{"w":"garrulous","p":"adj.","d":"talking too much about unimportant things","c":"喋喋不休的","s":"The garrulous taxi driver talked for the whole trip, but it was great listening practice for my Spanish.","t":"那位喋喋不休的計程車司機整趟車程都在說話，但這對我的西班牙文是很好的聽力練習。"},{"w":"glib","p":"adj.","d":"speaking easily but without thinking carefully","c":"油嘴滑舌的；隨口說的","s":"The politician gave a glib answer about education, so reporters asked him again for real details.","t":"那位政治人物對教育問題給了一個隨口敷衍的回答，所以記者再次追問具體細節。"},{"w":"hackneyed","p":"adj.","d":"used so often that it is no longer interesting","c":"陳腔濫調的","s":"\"At the end of the day\" is a hackneyed phrase, so try to find fresher words in your IELTS essay.","t":"「At the end of the day」是一個陳腔濫調的片語，所以在你的雅思作文中試著找更新鮮的字詞。"},{"w":"haughty","p":"adj.","d":"proud and unfriendly to others","c":"傲慢的","s":"The haughty waiter laughed at my French pronunciation, but the chef came out and kindly helped me order.","t":"那位傲慢的服務生嘲笑我的法文發音，但主廚走出來親切地幫我點餐。"},{"w":"impassive","p":"adj.","d":"showing no emotion","c":"面無表情的","s":"The interpreter kept an impassive face during the angry speech, because her job was to translate, not to react.","t":"口譯員在那場憤怒的演講中保持面無表情，因為她的工作是翻譯，而不是做出反應。"},{"w":"impertinent","p":"adj.","d":"rude and not showing respect","c":"無禮的；不禮貌的","s":"Asking someone's salary can seem impertinent in English-speaking countries, so it is better to avoid that question.","t":"在英語系國家詢問別人的薪水可能顯得無禮，所以最好避免那個問題。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (implacable – obtuse)","cards":[{"w":"implacable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to calm or change","c":"無法平息的；毫不妥協的","s":"The teacher was implacable about mobile phones, so any phone seen during the test was taken away until Friday.","t":"老師對手機毫不妥協，所以考試中被看到的任何手機都會被沒收到星期五。"},{"w":"inane","p":"adj.","d":"silly and without meaning","c":"愚蠢的；空洞的","s":"The chatbot gave an inane answer to my question, so I checked a real grammar book instead.","t":"聊天機器人對我的問題給了一個空洞的回答，所以我改去查一本真正的文法書。"},{"w":"incoherent","p":"adj.","d":"not clear or easy to understand","c":"語無倫次的；不連貫的","s":"He was so tired after the flight that his speech was incoherent, so we let him sleep before asking any more questions.","t":"他飛行後非常疲累，說話語無倫次，所以我們讓他先睡覺再問更多問題。"},{"w":"incorrigible","p":"adj.","d":"unable to be changed or improved","c":"無可救藥的；積習難改的","s":"My brother is an incorrigible joker, so even during serious family dinners he keeps making silly puns.","t":"我弟弟是個無可救藥的愛開玩笑者，所以即使在嚴肅的家庭晚餐上他也一直講冷雙關語。"},{"w":"incredulous","p":"adj.","d":"not able to believe something","c":"不相信的；懷疑的","s":"My friends were incredulous when I said I had learned Korean in one year, so I spoke to them in Korean to prove it.","t":"當我說我一年就學會韓文時，朋友們都不敢相信，所以我用韓文跟他們說話來證明。"},{"w":"indefatigable","p":"adj.","d":"never getting tired","c":"不知疲倦的","s":"The indefatigable volunteer taught Chinese to refugees every evening, and she still came to work early the next morning.","t":"那位不知疲倦的志工每天晚上教難民中文，而且隔天早上仍然提早上班。"},{"w":"ineffable","p":"adj.","d":"too great to be described in words","c":"難以言喻的","s":"Standing on the mountain at sunrise gave me an ineffable feeling, so I just stayed quiet and took no photos.","t":"日出時站在山上給了我一種難以言喻的感覺，所以我只是靜靜地待著，沒有拍照。"},{"w":"infallible","p":"adj.","d":"never wrong","c":"絕對正確的；萬無一失的","s":"Translation apps are useful but not infallible, so you should check important documents with a real person.","t":"翻譯應用程式很有用但並非萬無一失，所以重要文件應該找真人確認。"},{"w":"ingenuous","p":"adj.","d":"innocent and trusting","c":"天真的；坦率的","s":"The child's ingenuous question about why adults lie made everyone at the table laugh, but it also made us think.","t":"那孩子問大人為什麼說謊這個天真的問題讓餐桌上的每個人都笑了，但也讓我們陷入思考。"},{"w":"inscrutable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to understand or read","c":"難以理解的；高深莫測的","s":"The professor's inscrutable smile made us nervous, because we could not tell whether she liked our presentation.","t":"教授高深莫測的微笑讓我們很緊張，因為我們看不出她是否喜歡我們的報告。"},{"w":"insipid","p":"adj.","d":"without interest or flavour","c":"乏味的；枯燥的","s":"The textbook dialogues were insipid, so our teacher used real TV clips, and the class became much more lively.","t":"課本裡的對話很乏味，所以老師改用真實的電視片段，而課堂變得生動多了。"},{"w":"intransigent","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to change your opinion","c":"不妥協的；固執己見的","s":"The two sides were intransigent about the name of the new language school, so the meeting went on for four hours.","t":"雙方對新語言學校的名稱互不讓步，所以會議進行了四個小時。"},{"w":"irreverent","p":"adj.","d":"not showing respect for serious things","c":"不敬的；調侃的","s":"The comedian's irreverent jokes about grammar teachers were very popular, although a few teachers in the audience were not amused.","t":"那位喜劇演員對文法老師的調侃笑話很受歡迎，雖然觀眾中有幾位老師並不覺得好笑。"},{"w":"jocular","p":"adj.","d":"funny and joking","c":"詼諧的；愛開玩笑的","s":"Our principal gave a jocular speech at graduation, so the parents laughed and the nervous students relaxed.","t":"我們校長在畢業典禮上發表了一篇詼諧的演講，所以家長們笑了，緊張的學生也放鬆了。"},{"w":"laconic","p":"adj.","d":"using very few words","c":"簡潔的；寡言的","s":"My grandfather is laconic and usually answers with one word, but he tells long stories when he talks about his childhood.","t":"我爺爺話很少，通常只回答一個字，但談起童年時他會講很長的故事。"},{"w":"luminous","p":"adj.","d":"very bright or clear","c":"發光的；明亮清晰的","s":"Critics praised the luminous prose of the translation, because every sentence felt as clear and bright as the original.","t":"評論家讚揚譯本清澈明亮的文筆，因為每個句子都感覺和原著一樣清晰明亮。"},{"w":"magnanimous","p":"adj.","d":"kind and generous, especially to a rival","c":"寬宏大量的","s":"The champion was magnanimous after the debate, so she praised her opponent's arguments and shook hands warmly.","t":"冠軍在辯論賽後寬宏大量，她稱讚對手的論點並熱情地握手。"},{"w":"malevolent","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to harm others","c":"惡毒的；懷有惡意的","s":"The malevolent character in the story spreads lies in every village, but a young girl finally reveals the truth.","t":"故事中那個惡毒的角色在每個村莊散布謊言，但一個年輕女孩最終揭露了真相。"},{"w":"mendacious","p":"adj.","d":"not telling the truth","c":"說謊的；虛假的","s":"The advertisement made mendacious claims about learning English in a week, so many parents complained to the government.","t":"那則廣告做出一週學會英文的虛假聲明，所以許多家長向政府投訴。"},{"w":"mercurial","p":"adj.","d":"changing mood quickly and suddenly","c":"反覆無常的","s":"The director had a mercurial temper, so the actors never knew whether he would laugh or shout at them.","t":"導演的脾氣反覆無常，所以演員們永遠不知道他會笑還是對他們大吼。"},{"w":"morose","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy and quiet","c":"悶悶不樂的","s":"He was morose after failing the speaking test, but his teacher encouraged him, and he passed on his second try.","t":"他口說測驗不及格後悶悶不樂，但老師鼓勵他，而他第二次就通過了。"},{"w":"nebulous","p":"adj.","d":"unclear and not well defined","c":"模糊的；含糊不清的","s":"His plan to \"improve English\" was too nebulous, so his tutor asked him to set a clear goal for each week.","t":"他「提升英文」的計畫太模糊了，所以家教要求他為每週設定一個明確的目標。"},{"w":"nonchalant","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not worried","c":"若無其事的；漫不經心的","s":"She looked nonchalant before the interview, but she told me later that her hands were shaking under the table.","t":"她面試前看起來若無其事，但她後來告訴我，她的手在桌子底下發抖。"},{"w":"obsequious","p":"adj.","d":"too eager to please or obey","c":"諂媚的；奉承的","s":"The obsequious assistant agreed with everything the director said, so the bad ideas were never questioned.","t":"那位諂媚的助理附和導演說的每件事，所以那些糟糕的想法從未受到質疑。"},{"w":"obtuse","p":"adj.","d":"slow to understand","c":"遲鈍的","s":"I felt obtuse when I missed the joke in English, but my friend kindly explained the wordplay to me.","t":"當我沒聽懂英文笑話時覺得自己很遲鈍，但朋友親切地向我解釋了那個文字遊戲。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (ostentatious – urbane)","cards":[{"w":"ostentatious","p":"adj.","d":"showing off wealth or knowledge","c":"炫耀的；招搖的","s":"He used ostentatious words in every sentence to impress people, but most listeners just found him hard to understand.","t":"他每句話都用炫耀式的艱深字詞來給人留下印象，但大多數聽眾只覺得他很難懂。"},{"w":"petulant","p":"adj.","d":"childishly bad-tempered","c":"任性的；暴躁的","s":"The petulant boy threw his workbook on the floor, because he did not want to practise spelling any more.","t":"那個任性的男孩把作業簿丟到地上，因為他不想再練習拼字了。"},{"w":"poignant","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel sad and moved","c":"令人心酸的；感人的","s":"The film ends with a poignant letter from a soldier to his mother, and many people in the cinema started to cry.","t":"這部電影以一封士兵寫給母親的感人信件作結，而電影院裡許多人開始哭泣。"},{"w":"presumptuous","p":"adj.","d":"doing something without the right or permission","c":"冒昧的；放肆的","s":"It may seem presumptuous to call your professor by her first name, so wait until she invites you to do it.","t":"直接叫教授的名字可能顯得冒昧，所以要等她邀請你這麼做。"},{"w":"prosaic","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and without imagination","c":"平凡乏味的","s":"The poem was translated into prosaic language, so the beautiful images of the original were lost.","t":"這首詩被翻譯成平淡無奇的語言，所以原作中美麗的意象都消失了。"},{"w":"provincial","p":"adj.","d":"narrow-minded and not interested in the wider world","c":"眼界狹隘的；鄉土的","s":"Travelling abroad made her less provincial, because she learned that many cultures see the world differently.","t":"出國旅行讓她變得不那麼眼界狹隘，因為她了解到許多文化以不同方式看世界。"},{"w":"punctilious","p":"adj.","d":"very careful about details and rules","c":"一絲不苟的","s":"The editor is punctilious about commas, so she checks every page twice before the book goes to print.","t":"那位編輯對逗號一絲不苟，所以書付印前她會把每一頁檢查兩次。"},{"w":"raucous","p":"adj.","d":"loud and rough","c":"喧鬧的；刺耳的","s":"The raucous crowd at the night market made it hard to hear, so we had to shout our orders at the food stall.","t":"夜市喧鬧的人群讓人很難聽清楚，所以我們必須在小吃攤大聲喊出點餐內容。"},{"w":"recalcitrant","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to obey or cooperate","c":"頑抗的；不聽話的","s":"The recalcitrant printer refused to work all morning, so we had to hand in our essays by email instead.","t":"那台不聽使喚的印表機整個早上都不肯運作，所以我們只好改用電子郵件交作文。"},{"w":"replete","p":"adj.","d":"full of something","c":"充滿的","s":"Shakespeare's plays are replete with expressions we still use, like \"break the ice\" and \"wild-goose chase\".","t":"莎士比亞的戲劇充滿我們至今仍在使用的說法，例如「break the ice」和「wild-goose chase」。"},{"w":"reprehensible","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and deserving blame","c":"應受譴責的","s":"Copying a classmate's translation is reprehensible, so the teacher gave both students a zero and called their parents.","t":"抄襲同學的翻譯是應受譴責的，所以老師給兩名學生零分，並打電話給他們的家長。"},{"w":"sanguine","p":"adj.","d":"hopeful and positive","c":"樂觀的","s":"The coach is sanguine about the team's chances, but the players know they still need to train hard every day.","t":"教練對球隊的勝算很樂觀，但球員們知道他們每天仍需努力訓練。"},{"w":"sardonic","p":"adj.","d":"mocking in a cold, unkind way","c":"嘲諷的；冷嘲熱諷的","s":"He gave a sardonic smile when I mispronounced the word, so I felt embarrassed and stopped speaking.","t":"我唸錯那個字時他露出嘲諷的微笑，所以我覺得很尷尬，就不再說話了。"},{"w":"stoic","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not complaining in hard times","c":"堅忍的；淡然處之的","s":"She stayed stoic when her luggage was lost, and she calmly explained the problem in English to the airport staff.","t":"她的行李遺失時仍保持淡定，並冷靜地用英文向機場人員說明問題。"},{"w":"strident","p":"adj.","d":"loud, harsh and forceful","c":"刺耳的；強硬的","s":"The protesters made strident demands for bilingual road signs, and the city finally agreed to change them.","t":"抗議者強硬地要求設置雙語路標，而市政府最後同意更換。"},{"w":"sublime","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or excellent","c":"崇高的；絕妙的","s":"The singer's voice was sublime, so even people who did not understand Italian had tears in their eyes.","t":"那位歌手的嗓音美妙絕倫，所以即使不懂義大利文的人也眼含淚水。"},{"w":"subservient","p":"adj.","d":"too willing to obey others","c":"卑躬屈膝的；順從的","s":"In the old story the servant is always subservient, but the modern film shows him as brave and independent.","t":"在舊故事中那位僕人總是卑躬屈膝，但現代電影把他描繪成勇敢又獨立的人。"},{"w":"surreptitious","p":"adj.","d":"done secretly","c":"偷偷的；暗中的","s":"He made a surreptitious recording of the lecture, but the professor saw the phone and asked him to delete it.","t":"他偷偷地錄下講座內容，但教授看到手機並要求他刪除。"},{"w":"taciturn","p":"adj.","d":"not saying much","c":"沉默寡言的","s":"My taciturn classmate rarely speaks in class, but his written English is the best in our year.","t":"我那位沉默寡言的同學很少在課堂上說話，但他的英文寫作是我們年級最好的。"},{"w":"tangential","p":"adj.","d":"only slightly connected to the main topic","c":"離題的；關係不大的","s":"His answer was tangential to the question, so the examiner reminded him to focus on what was asked.","t":"他的回答和問題關係不大，所以考官提醒他專注在被問的內容上。"},{"w":"terse","p":"adj.","d":"very short and a little unfriendly","c":"簡短生硬的","s":"My manager sent a terse reply that only said \"Fix it\", so I wasn't sure whether she was angry.","t":"我的主管回了一則簡短生硬的訊息，只寫著「修好它」，所以我不確定她是否生氣了。"},{"w":"transitory","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only a short time","c":"短暫的","s":"Many slang words are transitory, and expressions that were popular ten years ago now sound very old-fashioned.","t":"許多俚語是短暫的，十年前流行的說法現在聽起來非常過時。"},{"w":"trenchant","p":"adj.","d":"clear, strong and direct in criticism","c":"一針見血的；尖銳的","s":"The editor's trenchant comments improved my article, although they hurt my feelings when I first read them.","t":"編輯一針見血的意見改善了我的文章，雖然我第一次讀時有點受傷。"},{"w":"unassuming","p":"adj.","d":"modest and not wanting attention","c":"謙遜的；不張揚的","s":"The unassuming old man in our neighbourhood never talks about himself, but he turned out to be a famous translator of Russian novels.","t":"我們社區裡那位不張揚的老先生從不談論自己，但他原來是一位知名的俄文小說譯者。"},{"w":"urbane","p":"adj.","d":"polite, confident and comfortable in social situations","c":"溫文爾雅的","s":"The urbane host made every guest feel welcome, and he switched easily between English, French and Chinese.","t":"那位溫文儒雅的主人讓每位客人都感到受歡迎，而且他能輕鬆地在英文、法文和中文之間切換。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (vapid – inculcate)","cards":[{"w":"vapid","p":"adj.","d":"boring and empty of ideas","c":"空洞乏味的","s":"The talk show was full of vapid chat about celebrities, so I switched to a documentary instead.","t":"那個脫口秀充滿了關於名人的空洞乏味的閒聊，所以我轉台去看紀錄片。"},{"w":"vicarious","p":"adj.","d":"felt by watching or reading about others","c":"間接體驗的；感同身受的","s":"Reading travel blogs gives me vicarious pleasure, because I can explore Peru without leaving my bedroom.","t":"閱讀旅遊部落格帶給我間接體驗的樂趣，因為我不用離開臥室就能探索秘魯。"},{"w":"virulent","p":"adj.","d":"extremely strong, harmful or full of hate","c":"猛烈的；惡毒的","s":"The singer received virulent attacks online, but she replied calmly and asked her fans to be kind.","t":"那位歌手在網路上遭受惡毒的攻擊，但她冷靜地回應，並請粉絲們保持善意。"},{"w":"vitriolic","p":"adj.","d":"full of bitter, angry criticism","c":"尖酸刻薄的","s":"The vitriolic letter to the newspaper attacked the new language policy, but the editor still decided to print it.","t":"那封寫給報社的尖酸刻薄的信抨擊新的語言政策，但編輯仍決定刊登。"},{"w":"whimsical","p":"adj.","d":"playful and unusual","c":"異想天開的；古怪有趣的","s":"The children's book has a whimsical style, so the translator invented new silly words to keep the fun in Chinese.","t":"這本童書有一種古怪有趣的風格，所以譯者創造了新的傻氣字詞來保留中文版的趣味。"},{"w":"wistful","p":"adj.","d":"sadly wishing for something","c":"惆悵的；渴望的","s":"My grandmother gave a wistful smile when she heard the old song, because it reminded her of her school days.","t":"奶奶聽到那首老歌時露出惆悵的微笑，因為那讓她想起了學生時代。"},{"w":"intercultural","p":"adj.","d":"between different cultures","c":"跨文化的","s":"The exchange programme improves intercultural skills, so students learn how to work with people who have very different habits.","t":"這個交換計畫能提升跨文化能力，所以學生學會如何與習慣非常不同的人合作。"},{"w":"cross-cultural","p":"adj.","d":"involving two or more cultures","c":"跨文化的","s":"Eye contact can cause cross-cultural misunderstandings, because it seems polite in some countries but rude in others.","t":"眼神接觸可能造成跨文化的誤解，因為它在某些國家顯得禮貌，在其他國家卻顯得無禮。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings clearly","c":"富有表現力的","s":"Italian speakers are often very expressive with their hands, so you can sometimes guess their meaning without words.","t":"說義大利語的人常常用手勢表達得很生動，所以有時不用言語你也能猜出他們的意思。"},{"w":"parochial","p":"adj.","d":"only interested in your own small area","c":"狹隘的；地方性的","s":"His views on language were rather parochial, but living abroad for a year opened his mind to new ideas.","t":"他對語言的看法相當狹隘，但在國外生活一年讓他對新想法敞開了心胸。"},{"w":"monolithic","p":"adj.","d":"large and all the same, without variety","c":"單一龐大的；鐵板一塊的","s":"English is not a monolithic language, because people in Scotland, India and Jamaica all speak it in very different ways.","t":"英文並不是單一不變的語言，因為蘇格蘭、印度和牙買加的人說英文的方式都非常不同。"},{"w":"pluralistic","p":"adj.","d":"accepting many different groups and views","c":"多元的","s":"Taiwan is becoming more pluralistic, so public announcements on the MRT are now made in four different languages.","t":"台灣正變得更加多元，所以捷運上的公共廣播現在用四種不同的語言播報。"},{"w":"accede","p":"v.","d":"to agree to a request","c":"同意；應允","s":"The school accede to the parents' request, so Japanese is now offered as an after-school class.","t":"學校同意了家長的請求，所以現在日文被列為課後課程。"},{"w":"adjudicate","p":"v.","d":"to judge officially","c":"裁決；評判","s":"Three teachers adjudicate the English speech contest, and they gave marks for content, pronunciation and confidence.","t":"三位老師評判這場英文演講比賽，而他們針對內容、發音和自信心給分。"},{"w":"append","p":"v.","d":"to add something at the end","c":"附加","s":"Please append a short glossary to your report, so readers can check the technical terms quickly.","t":"請在你的報告後附加一份簡短的詞彙表，好讓讀者能快速查閱專業術語。"},{"w":"apprise","p":"v.","d":"to inform someone","c":"告知；通知","s":"The airline apprise passengers of the delay in three languages, but many people still missed the announcement.","t":"航空公司用三種語言通知乘客班機延誤，但許多人仍錯過了廣播。"},{"w":"berate","p":"v.","d":"to scold someone angrily","c":"嚴厲斥責","s":"The coach berate the players for their careless mistakes, but later he apologised for shouting so loudly.","t":"教練嚴厲斥責球員們粗心的失誤，但後來他為大聲吼叫道歉。"},{"w":"cajole","p":"v.","d":"to persuade someone with gentle words","c":"哄騙；勸誘","s":"My mum cajole my little brother into reading an English book, because she promised him ice cream afterwards.","t":"我媽媽哄我弟弟讀一本英文書，因為她答應他之後給他冰淇淋。"},{"w":"codify","p":"v.","d":"to arrange rules into a written system","c":"編纂；系統化","s":"Early dictionary makers tried to codify English spelling, but many strange spellings were already too common to change.","t":"早期的字典編纂者試圖把英文拼字系統化，但許多奇怪的拼法已經太普遍而無法改變。"},{"w":"demur","p":"v.","d":"to show you don't agree","c":"表示異議；猶豫","s":"The manager suggested working on Sunday, but several staff demur, so the meeting was moved to Monday.","t":"經理建議星期天加班，但好幾位員工表示異議，所以會議改到星期一。"},{"w":"deprecate","p":"v.","d":"to express disapproval of something","c":"不贊成；反對","s":"Some teachers deprecate the use of translation apps in class, but others think they can be useful if used carefully.","t":"有些老師不贊成在課堂上使用翻譯應用程式，但其他老師認為若謹慎使用會很有用。"},{"w":"explicate","p":"v.","d":"to explain something in detail","c":"詳細解釋","s":"The professor took an hour to explicate one short poem, and she showed us how every word carried hidden meaning.","t":"教授花了一小時詳細解釋一首短詩，而她讓我們看到每個字如何承載隱藏的意思。"},{"w":"imbue","p":"v.","d":"to fill with a feeling or quality","c":"使充滿；灌輸","s":"Her grandparents imbue her with a love of Taiwanese folk songs, so she now sings them at local festivals.","t":"她的祖父母讓她充滿對台灣民謠的熱愛，所以她現在會在地方節慶中演唱。"},{"w":"implore","p":"v.","d":"to ask someone desperately","c":"懇求；哀求","s":"The lost tourist implore us to help him find his hotel, so we called the front desk and explained in Chinese.","t":"那位迷路的觀光客懇求我們幫他找飯店，所以我們打給櫃台並用中文說明。"},{"w":"inculcate","p":"v.","d":"to teach an idea by repeating it often","c":"反覆灌輸","s":"Good teachers inculcate a habit of reading every day, because regular reading builds vocabulary better than lists.","t":"好老師會反覆灌輸每天閱讀的習慣，因為規律閱讀比背單字表更能增加詞彙量。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (intersperse – mellifluous)","cards":[{"w":"intersperse","p":"v.","d":"to put things here and there among other things","c":"點綴；散布","s":"The speaker intersperse her talk with funny stories, so the audience stayed interested for the whole hour.","t":"講者在演講中穿插好笑的故事，所以觀眾整整一小時都保持興趣。"},{"w":"liaise","p":"v.","d":"to work with and share information with others","c":"聯絡；協調","s":"The translator will liaise with the Japanese team, so our manager does not need to send emails in Japanese.","t":"譯者將與日本團隊聯絡協調，所以我們經理不需要用日文寄電子郵件。"},{"w":"mollify","p":"v.","d":"to make someone less angry","c":"平息；安撫","s":"The waiter tried to mollify the angry customer with a free dessert, and he apologised in careful English.","t":"服務生試著用一份免費甜點安撫那位生氣的顧客，並用謹慎的英文道歉。"},{"w":"obviate","p":"v.","d":"to remove the need for something","c":"免除；使不必要","s":"Clear instructions obviate the need for long explanations, so the workers can start the task right away.","t":"清楚的說明能免除冗長解釋的需要，所以工人能立刻開始工作。"},{"w":"promulgate","p":"v.","d":"to make an idea or law widely known","c":"頒布；宣傳推廣","s":"The ministry promulgate a new spelling guide for schools, and teachers had to learn the changes over the summer.","t":"教育部頒布了一份新的學校拼寫指南，而老師們必須在暑假學會這些改變。"},{"w":"prevaricate","p":"v.","d":"to avoid giving a direct answer","c":"支吾搪塞","s":"When the reporter asked about the error, the spokesman began to prevaricate, so everyone suspected he was hiding something.","t":"當記者問到那個錯誤時，發言人開始支吾其詞，所以大家懷疑他在隱瞞什麼。"},{"w":"transpose","p":"v.","d":"to change the order or position of things","c":"調換；移調","s":"Learners sometimes transpose two letters when they type quickly, so \"form\" and \"from\" are a common mix-up.","t":"學習者打字很快時有時會把兩個字母對調，所以「form」和「from」是常見的混淆。"},{"w":"vacillate","p":"v.","d":"to keep changing your mind","c":"猶豫不決；搖擺不定","s":"I vacillate between studying Spanish and Japanese for months, but in the end I chose Japanese because of anime.","t":"我在學西班牙文和日文之間搖擺不定好幾個月，但最後因為動漫選了日文。"},{"w":"vex","p":"v.","d":"to annoy or worry someone","c":"使煩惱；使惱火","s":"English spelling continues to vex students, because so many words are not written the way they sound.","t":"英文拼字持續困擾學生，因為許多字的寫法和發音不一樣。"},{"w":"antagonise","p":"v.","d":"to make someone angry or unfriendly","c":"激怒；使對立","s":"Try not to antagonise your teammates by correcting their English in front of everyone, because it can be embarrassing.","t":"試著不要在大家面前糾正隊友的英文而激怒他們，因為那可能令人難堪。"},{"w":"atone","p":"v.","d":"to do something to make up for a wrong","c":"贖罪；彌補","s":"He wanted to atone for his rude comments, so he wrote a long apology to his host family in their language.","t":"他想彌補自己無禮的言論，所以他用寄宿家庭的語言寫了一封長長的道歉信。"},{"w":"circumscribe","p":"v.","d":"to limit something","c":"限制","s":"The new rules circumscribe the use of phones during class, but students may still use dictionaries on them.","t":"新規定限制課堂上使用手機，但學生仍可用手機查字典。"},{"w":"gainsay","p":"v.","d":"to deny or disagree with something","c":"否認；反駁","s":"Nobody can gainsay the value of reading, but many students still prefer watching short videos.","t":"沒有人能否認閱讀的價值，但許多學生仍偏好看短影片。"},{"w":"rephrase","p":"v.","d":"to say something again using different words","c":"換個說法","s":"If the examiner does not understand you, rephrase your idea in simpler words, and keep talking calmly.","t":"如果考官聽不懂你的話，就用更簡單的字換個說法，並保持冷靜繼續說。"},{"w":"reword","p":"v.","d":"to change the words of a text","c":"改寫措辭","s":"The company had to reword its new advertisement, because the direct translation sounded quite rude to customers in Spanish.","t":"這家公司必須改寫新廣告的措辭，因為直接翻譯成西班牙文後對顧客來說聽起來相當無禮。"},{"w":"interchangeably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that one can replace the other","c":"可互換地","s":"People often use \"big\" and \"large\" interchangeably, but we say \"a big mistake\" much more often than \"a large mistake\".","t":"人們常常互換使用「big」和「large」，但我們說「a big mistake」比「a large mistake」頻繁得多。"},{"w":"expressly","p":"adv.","d":"clearly and on purpose","c":"明確地；特意地","s":"The exam rules expressly say that phones are not allowed, so the student who used one received a zero.","t":"考試規則明確規定不得使用手機，所以那名使用手機的學生得了零分。"},{"w":"loosely","p":"adv.","d":"not exactly","c":"大致地；不嚴格地","s":"The film is loosely based on a true story, so many events and characters were changed for the screen.","t":"這部電影是大致根據真實故事改編的，所以許多事件和角色都為了銀幕而改動。"},{"w":"strictly","p":"adv.","d":"exactly and completely","c":"嚴格地","s":"strictly speaking, a tomato is a fruit, but most people still put it in salads and call it a vegetable.","t":"嚴格來說，番茄是一種水果，但大多數人仍然把它放進沙拉並稱它為蔬菜。"},{"w":"clarification","p":"n.","d":"an explanation that makes something clearer","c":"澄清；說明","s":"If you don't understand a question in the interview, ask for clarification, because guessing may lead to a wrong answer.","t":"如果你在面試中聽不懂問題，就要求澄清，因為瞎猜可能導致錯誤的回答。"},{"w":"relatable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to understand because it is like your own life","c":"能引起共鳴的","s":"The novel's teenage hero is very relatable, so young readers in many countries see themselves in her problems.","t":"這部小說的青少年主角非常能引起共鳴，所以許多國家的年輕讀者都在她的問題中看見自己。"},{"w":"cadence","p":"n.","d":"the rise and fall of the voice when speaking","c":"抑揚頓挫；語調節奏","s":"The poet read with a gentle cadence, so even listeners who did not know Welsh enjoyed the sound of her words.","t":"詩人用柔和的抑揚頓挫朗讀，所以即使不懂威爾斯語的聽眾也很享受她話語的聲音。"},{"w":"gesticulate","p":"v.","d":"to move your hands while talking","c":"比手畫腳","s":"When we could not find the right words, we gesticulate wildly, and the market seller finally understood that we wanted mangoes.","t":"當我們找不到適當的字時，就拼命比手畫腳，而市場攤販終於明白我們想要芒果。"},{"w":"loquacious","p":"adj.","d":"talking a lot","c":"健談的；多話的","s":"My loquacious neighbour talks to me in English every morning, so my speaking has improved without any classes.","t":"我那位健談的鄰居每天早上都和我用英文聊天，所以我沒上任何課口說就進步了。"},{"w":"mellifluous","p":"adj.","d":"sweet and smooth to hear","c":"（聲音）甜美流暢的","s":"The radio host has a mellifluous voice, so many listeners say they feel calm while they drive to work.","t":"那位廣播主持人有著甜美圓潤的嗓音，所以許多聽眾說他們開車上班時感覺很平靜。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (moribund – charisma)","cards":[{"w":"moribund","p":"adj.","d":"close to dying or ending","c":"垂死的；瀕臨消亡的","s":"The language was moribund by 1990, but a new school programme has brought hundreds of young speakers back.","t":"這種語言到 1990 年時已瀕臨消亡，但一個新的學校計畫已帶回了數百名年輕使用者。"},{"w":"pithy","p":"adj.","d":"short but full of meaning","c":"精闢的；簡潔有力的","s":"The teacher wrote a pithy comment on my essay, and those few words helped me more than a long report.","t":"老師在我的作文上寫了一句精闢的評語，而那寥寥幾個字比長篇報告更能幫助我。"},{"w":"quip","p":"n.","d":"a short, clever joke","c":"妙語；俏皮話","s":"The interpreter could not translate the president's quip about cheese, so she simply told the audience it was a joke.","t":"口譯員無法翻譯總統關於起司的俏皮話，所以她只好告訴觀眾那是個笑話。"},{"w":"repartee","p":"n.","d":"quick and clever replies in conversation","c":"機智應答","s":"The two hosts are famous for their repartee, but they say it took years of practice to sound so natural.","t":"兩位主持人以機智的對答聞名，但他們說花了好幾年練習才能聽起來那麼自然。"},{"w":"verbiage","p":"n.","d":"too many unnecessary words","c":"冗詞贅字","s":"Cut the verbiage from your essay, because examiners prefer clear points to long sentences that say very little.","t":"刪掉你文章中的冗詞贅字，因為考官偏好清楚的論點，而不是說了很少內容的長句。"},{"w":"voluble","p":"adj.","d":"talking a lot and quickly","c":"健談的；滔滔不絕的","s":"The voluble tour guide explained every building in fast English, so we had to ask her to slow down.","t":"那位滔滔不絕的導遊用很快的英文解說每棟建築，所以我們只好請她說慢一點。"},{"w":"wry","p":"adj.","d":"showing amused but slightly annoyed humour","c":"苦笑的；挖苦的","s":"He gave a wry smile when the app translated his name as \"fried egg\", but he still showed it to his friends.","t":"當應用程式把他的名字翻成「煎蛋」時，他露出苦笑，但他還是拿給朋友看。"},{"w":"peruse","p":"v.","d":"to read something carefully","c":"細讀；仔細閱讀","s":"Please peruse the contract before you sign it, because the English version and the Chinese version may differ.","t":"簽約前請仔細閱讀合約，因為英文版和中文版可能有出入。"},{"w":"opine","p":"v.","d":"to give your opinion","c":"發表意見","s":"Many people opine online about the \"correct\" way to speak, but linguists say every variety has its own rules.","t":"許多人在網路上發表意見談論「正確」的說話方式，但語言學家說每種語言變體都有自己的規則。"},{"w":"pundit","p":"n.","d":"an expert who gives opinions in the media","c":"專家；評論員","s":"A TV pundit claimed that young people cannot write properly any more, but the research shows a different picture.","t":"一位電視評論員聲稱年輕人已經不會好好寫作了，但研究呈現出不同的情況。"},{"w":"germane","p":"adj.","d":"relevant to the subject","c":"密切相關的","s":"Your story about your holiday is interesting, but it is not germane to the essay question, so please remove it.","t":"你關於假期的故事很有趣，但和作文題目並不相關，所以請把它刪掉。"},{"w":"flippant","p":"adj.","d":"not serious when you should be","c":"輕率的；不認真的","s":"His flippant answer about climate change annoyed the examiner, so he lost marks for not taking the topic seriously.","t":"他對氣候變遷輕率的回答惹惱了考官，所以他因為沒有認真看待題目而被扣分。"},{"w":"genial","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and cheerful","c":"親切友好的；和藹的","s":"The genial old professor invited international students to his home, and he cooked dishes from each of their countries.","t":"那位和藹的老教授邀請國際學生到他家，還煮了他們每個人國家的菜。"},{"w":"cordial","p":"adj.","d":"warm and polite","c":"熱誠的；誠懇的","s":"The two leaders had a cordial meeting, and their interpreters said the conversation went smoothly from start to finish.","t":"兩位領袖進行了一場誠懇友好的會談，而他們的口譯員說對話從頭到尾都很順利。"},{"w":"edify","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone in a way that improves their mind","c":"啟發；教誨","s":"The museum's language exhibition is designed to edify visitors, but it is also full of fun games for children.","t":"博物館的語言展旨在啟發參觀者，但它也充滿了給孩子玩的有趣遊戲。"},{"w":"epiphany","p":"n.","d":"a sudden moment of understanding","c":"頓悟","s":"I had an epiphany when I realised that English \"the\" works a bit like pointing, and after that articles felt much easier.","t":"當我明白英文的「the」有點像用手指東西時，我突然頓悟了，從那之後冠詞感覺容易多了。"},{"w":"exuberant","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and happiness","c":"活力充沛的；熱情洋溢的","s":"The exuberant children sang the English song loudly, and their parents filmed the performance on their phones.","t":"那些活力充沛的孩子大聲唱著英文歌，而他們的父母用手機錄下了表演。"},{"w":"misgiving","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of doubt or worry","c":"疑慮；擔憂","s":"I had some misgiving about studying abroad alone, but the friendly people there soon made me feel at home.","t":"我對獨自出國念書有些疑慮，但那裡友善的人們很快讓我感覺像在家一樣。"},{"w":"qualm","p":"n.","d":"an uneasy feeling that you are doing wrong","c":"不安；顧慮","s":"She had no qualm about asking strangers for directions, so her French improved very quickly in Paris.","t":"她對向陌生人問路毫無顧慮，所以她的法文在巴黎進步得非常快。"},{"w":"vehement","p":"adj.","d":"showing strong feeling","c":"激烈的；強烈的","s":"There was vehement opposition to closing the language centre, so hundreds of students signed a petition.","t":"關閉語言中心遭到強烈的反對，所以有數百名學生連署請願。"},{"w":"unabashed","p":"adj.","d":"not ashamed or embarrassed","c":"毫不掩飾的；不害臊的","s":"He is an unabashed fan of K-pop, and he proudly sings Korean songs at every school party.","t":"他是一個毫不掩飾的 K-pop 迷，而且他在每場學校派對上都自豪地唱韓文歌。"},{"w":"pensive","p":"adj.","d":"thinking deeply, often a little sadly","c":"沉思的","s":"She looked pensive as she read her grandfather's old letters, because she was trying to imagine his life in the 1950s.","t":"她讀著爺爺的舊信時看起來若有所思，因為她正試著想像他在 1950 年代的生活。"},{"w":"solemn","p":"adj.","d":"serious and formal","c":"莊嚴的；嚴肅的","s":"The ceremony was solemn, so the students stood silently while the national anthem played in two languages.","t":"典禮很莊嚴，所以學生們靜靜站立，國歌以兩種語言播放。"},{"w":"camaraderie","p":"n.","d":"friendship and trust among a group","c":"友誼；同袍情誼","s":"There was real camaraderie in our language class, because we laughed at our mistakes together and helped each other study.","t":"我們的語言班有真正的同儕情誼，因為我們一起笑看自己的錯誤，也互相幫助讀書。"},{"w":"charisma","p":"n.","d":"a strong personal charm that attracts people","c":"領袖魅力；個人魅力","s":"The speaker had so much charisma that people listened to every word, even though her English was not perfect.","t":"那位講者極具個人魅力，以致人們專心聽她說的每一個字，即使她的英文並不完美。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"lost for words","p":"adj.phr.","d":"so surprised or moved that you cannot speak","c":"驚訝得說不出話","s":"I was lost for words when my students surprised me with a cake, so I just smiled and hugged them all.","t":"當學生們用蛋糕給我驚喜時，我感動得說不出話，所以我只是微笑並擁抱了他們每一個人。"},{"w":"in other words","p":"phr.","d":"used to say something again more simply","c":"換句話說","s":"The test is \"not compulsory\"; in other words, you can choose not to take it, but most students take it anyway.","t":"這個考試「並非強制」；換句話說，你可以選擇不考，但大多數學生還是會去考。"},{"w":"have a way with words","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be good at speaking or writing","c":"很會說話；文筆好","s":"My sister have a way with words, so she always writes the birthday cards for our family.","t":"我姊姊很會遣詞用字，所以我們家的生日卡片總是由她來寫。"},{"w":"not mince one's words","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak very directly, even if it is unkind","c":"說話直截了當","s":"My coach does not mince one's words, so when I play badly he tells me exactly what I did wrong.","t":"我的教練說話直截了當，所以當我表現不好時，他會確切告訴我哪裡做錯了。"},{"w":"have the last word","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make the final comment in an argument","c":"說最後一句話","s":"My little brother always wants to have the last word, so our arguments go on until Mum tells us to stop.","t":"我弟弟總是想說最後一句話，所以我們的爭吵會一直持續到媽媽叫我們停止為止。"},{"w":"word for word","p":"adv.","d":"in exactly the same words","c":"一字不差地；逐字地","s":"Don't copy the article word for word, because your teacher wants you to explain the ideas in your own words.","t":"不要逐字照抄那篇文章，因為老師希望你用自己的話來解釋這些想法。"},{"w":"it's all Greek to me","p":"phr.","d":"I cannot understand this at all","c":"我完全看不懂","s":"My dad showed me his tax forms, but it's all Greek to me, so I told him to ask an accountant.","t":"我爸爸給我看他的報稅表，但我完全看不懂，所以我叫他去問會計師。"},{"w":"speak the same language","p":"v.phr.","d":"to share similar ideas and understand each other","c":"想法一致；有共同語言","s":"The designer and the engineer finally speak the same language, so the project moved much faster after that meeting.","t":"設計師和工程師終於有了共同語言，所以那次會議之後計畫進展得快多了。"},{"w":"the gift of the gab","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ability to speak easily and persuasively","c":"好口才","s":"Our class president has the gift of the gab, so she can talk the teachers into almost anything.","t":"我們班長有好口才，所以她幾乎可以說服老師答應任何事。"},{"w":"tongue-tied","p":"adj.","d":"unable to speak because you are nervous","c":"緊張得說不出話","s":"I was tongue-tied when I met my favourite singer, so I just stood there and forgot every English word I knew.","t":"當我見到最喜歡的歌手時，我緊張得說不出話，所以我只是站在那裡，忘光了我會的每一個英文字。"},{"w":"a slip of the tongue","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small mistake when you are speaking","c":"口誤","s":"Calling my teacher \"Mum\" was a slip of the tongue, but the whole class laughed for five minutes.","t":"叫老師「媽媽」只是一個口誤，但全班笑了五分鐘。"},{"w":"bite one's tongue","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from saying something","c":"忍住不說","s":"I wanted to correct my boss's English, but I bite one's tongue, because the meeting was not the right time.","t":"我想糾正老闆的英文，但我忍住沒說，因為會議中不是適當的時機。"},{"w":"mind one's language","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be careful not to use rude words","c":"說話注意用詞","s":"Please mind one's language in front of the children, because they copy every word they hear.","t":"請在孩子面前注意你的用詞，因為他們會模仿聽到的每一個字。"},{"w":"pick up a language","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn a language naturally without formal study","c":"自然學會一種語言","s":"Young kids can pick up a language quickly when they play with local children, while adults often need classes.","t":"小孩和當地孩子一起玩時能很快地自然學會一種語言，而大人常常需要上課。"},{"w":"get by in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to know just enough of a language to manage","c":"勉強應付（某語言）","s":"I can get by in Japanese when I travel, but I cannot understand the news or have deep conversations.","t":"我旅行時能用日文勉強應付，但我聽不懂新聞，也無法深入交談。"},{"w":"break the ice","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people feel relaxed when they first meet","c":"打破僵局；破冰","s":"Our teacher played a name game to break the ice on the first day, and soon everyone was chatting and laughing.","t":"老師在第一天玩了一個名字遊戲來破冰，很快大家就聊天說笑起來了。"},{"w":"talk at cross purposes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to misunderstand each other because you mean different things","c":"雞同鴨講","s":"We talk at cross purposes for ten minutes, because I meant the train station while she meant the bus station.","t":"我們雞同鴨講了十分鐘，因為我指的是火車站，而她指的是公車站。"},{"w":"actions speak louder than words","p":"phr.","d":"what you do matters more than what you say","c":"行動勝於言語","s":"He promised to practise English every day, but actions speak louder than words, so I'll believe it when I see it.","t":"他答應每天練習英文，但行動勝於言語，所以等我親眼看到才會相信。"},{"w":"put words into someone's mouth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say that someone said something they did not","c":"曲解別人的話；硬說別人說過","s":"Please don't put words into someone's mouth, because I never said that your translation was bad.","t":"請不要硬說我說過那些話，因為我從來沒說你的翻譯很糟。"},{"w":"speak volumes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show something clearly without words","c":"說明一切；意味深長","s":"Her silence speak volumes after the argument, so I knew I had to apologise before dinner.","t":"爭吵後她的沉默說明了一切，所以我知道我必須在晚餐前道歉。"}]}];
